{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c593","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":292,"recorded_at":1780531400000579,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcb9f2370e1938ba32c1e735d5c","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(625 line(s) above)\n626|### 2.4 Execution profiles\n627|\n628|The persisted profile enum is <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code>.\n629|<code>yolo</code> means the provider-specific unrestricted/no-approval mode; it\n630|does not mean that <code>ax</code> ignores its own ownership, conflict,\n631|allowlist, or integrity checks.\n632|\n633|The immutable Session Record stores the creation profile. Every\n634|<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n635|<code>session.resumed</code>, and <code>fork.created</code> event repeats the\n636|effective ax profile and the digest of the authoritative\n637|<code>profile.changed</code> event from which it was derived, or null when the\n638|Session Record is still the authority. A profile change requires\n639|<code>ax session set-profile NAME PROFILE</code>, a new event under the current\n640|lease, and operator confirmation when changing to <code>yolo</code>. A resume\n641|MUST fail with <code>profile_mapping_unavailable</code> if the adapter cannot\n642|map the stored profile for the probed provider version.\n643|\n644|The effective persisted profile is the Session Record value followed by the\n645|newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in lease/sequence order.\n646|Losing-lease or ambiguous events MUST NOT change it. Every command that says\n647|“persisted profile” refers to this derived value. The profile source is null\n648|when no authoritative change exists and otherwise is exactly that newest\n649|event's <code>event_id</code>. A Checkpoint's event-head closure fixes both\n650|values for that checkpoint; a bundle, resume, or fork MUST NOT fall back to the\n651|Session Record creation value when the closure contains a later change.\n652|\n653|Fork creates a new authority boundary. Its new Session Record stores the\n654|source-checkpoint effective profile as its creation profile, so the new\n655|session's <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null. The\n656|<code>fork.created.source_profile_event_id</code> separately preserves the\n657|nullable source-session event used for that projection; it is provenance and\n658|MUST NOT be treated as a profile event in the new session's event chain.\n659|\n660|Provider mapping is evidence, not profile authority. In particular, Pi 0.73.1\n661|maps both ax profiles to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code>; the two ax\n662|profiles remain distinct because the Session/Event authority and confirmation\n663|history remain distinct even when the provider mapping strings are equal.\n664|\n665|The following end-to-end profile fixtures are normative. Let P0 be the Session\n666|Record profile, E1 an authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event to P1,\n667|and C1 a checkpoint whose event-head closure contains E1:\n668|\n669|| Fixture | Path | Required profile authority |\n670|| --- | --- | --- |\n671|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-TAKEOVER</code> | Direct start P0 → E1 → C1 → graceful/force takeover | Bundle is absent; materialization finalize, plugin resume, and resumed event all carry P1/E1 |\n672|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME</code> | Direct stop at C1 → owner resume | Plugin resume and resumed event carry P1/E1; creation P0 is ignored |\n673|| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-FORK</code> | Fork C1 | New Session Record creation profile is P1; fork event carries P1/null as new-session authority plus <code>source_profile_event_id=E1</code>; resumed carries P1/null |\n674|| <code>PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER</code> | Task-board start P0 → E1 → export C1 → takeover | Bundle projection carries P1/E1; journaled bridge resume and events use the same pair |\n675|| <code>PROFILE-TB-RESUME</code> | Task-board owner resume from C1 | Bundle, bridge resume, and events agree on P1/E1 |\n676|| <code>PROFILE-TB-FORK</code> | Task-board fork C1 | Source bundle carries P1/E1; new Session Record and bridge resume use P1/null; fork event retains E1 only in <code>source_profile_event_id</code> |\n677|| <code>PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING</code> | Pi changes <code>standard</code> to <code>yolo</code> at E1 while both map to <code>default_unrestricted_tool_set</code> | Ax still persists and reports P1/E1; equal provider argv text is not authority to erase E1 |\n678|\n679|Any fixture that uses P0 after C1, omits E1 where the event schema requires its\n680|source, or accepts a bundle profile inconsistent with C1 is\n681|<code>integrity_failure</code> before activation.\n682|\n683|## 3. Architecture and durable local layout\n684|\n685|### 3.1 Required components\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c595","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":293,"recorded_at":1780531400000581,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcba14475c595c211817d622a09","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3490 line(s) above)\n3491|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3492|\n3493|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3494|\n3495|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3496|| --- | --- |\n3497|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3498|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3499|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n3500|| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\n3501|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3502|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3503|\n3504|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3505|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3506|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3507|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3508|probe accepts them.\n3509|\n3510|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3511|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3512|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3513|confirmation controls still apply.\n3514|\n3515|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3516|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3517|\n3518|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3519|\n3520|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3521|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3522|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3523|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3524|\n3525|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3526|| --- | --- |\n3527|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3528|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3529|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3530|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3531|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3532|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3533|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3534|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3535|\n3536|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3537|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3538|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3539|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3540|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3541|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3542|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3543|\n3544|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3545|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3546|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3547|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3548|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3549|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3550|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3551|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3552|\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3556|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3557|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3558|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3559|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3560|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3561|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3562|\n3563|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3564|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3565|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3566|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3567|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3568|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3569|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3570|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
