{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":318,"recorded_at":1780531400000631,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcb-b222-7782-86eb-df4da111537b"},"task_id":"01a0adcb-b222-7782-86eb-df4da111537b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adcb-b222-7782-86eb-df4da111537b","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(2084 line(s) above)\n2085|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2086|\n2087|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2088|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2089|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2090|\n2091|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2092|| --- | --- | --- |\n2093|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Provider Identity schema identifier |\n2094|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2095|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2096|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2097|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing logical session |\n2098|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id | Must equal the Session Record provider |\n2099|| <code>provider_version</code> | string[1..128] | Exact probed version |\n2100|| <code>provider_version_range</code> | string[1..256] | Adapter compatibility range used for this identity |\n2101|| <code>native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] | Opaque provider handle; never interpreted by core |\n2102|| <code>identity_kind</code> | enum | <code>session_uuid</code>, <code>session_path_or_id</code>, <code>backend_conversation_uuid</code>, <code>task_board_managed</code>, or <code>provider_defined</code> |\n2103|| <code>logical_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Member of the Session Record workspace group |\n2104|| <code>backend_realm_fingerprint</code> | digest or null | Non-secret fingerprint; non-null when backend/account realm is a resume precondition |\n2105|| <code>opaque_identity</code> | map(provider-identity-key,string[1..1024])[0..32] | Explicit adapter data map defined below |\n2106|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Identifying owner host |\n2107|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2108|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2109|\n2110|A provider-identity key matches <code>[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}</code>. Map keys\n2111|are data rather than schema members; values are non-secret strings only. This\n2112|is the sole provider-defined identity-data surface in version 1.0.0. It MUST\n2113|NOT contain an absolute path, credential, environment value, PID, socket,\n2114|terminal ID, or mutable cache selector. Structured or binary provider data\n2115|belongs in a content-addressed provider manifest, not this map.\n2116|\n2117|An absolute workspace path MAY appear only as source observation metadata. It\n2118|MUST NOT be part of the cross-host identity. The destination adapter MUST\n2119|derive native path keys from the destination workspace mapping.\n2120|\n2121|Normative negative fixtures are: unknown <code>identity_kind</code>; absent\n2122|<code>opaque_identity</code>; a map value that is an object instead of a\n2123|string; an absolute source path in that map; or an Antigravity\n2124|<code>backend_conversation_uuid</code> with null realm fingerprint. Each MUST\n2125|fail schema or provider-identity validation. A backend fingerprint is optional\n2126|for the other kinds unless that provider's Section 8 contract requires it.\n2127|\n2128|Normative example:\n2129|\n2130|~~~json\n2131|{\n2132|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n2133|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2134|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:c879d766da67a8cfb3a3f6eae2234faa5d52d8df987496eae2218f40e5e220c2\",\n2135|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2136|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2137|  \"provider_id\": \"antigravity\",\n2138|  \"provider_version\": \"1.1.14\",\n2139|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=1.1.14 <1.2.0\",\n2140|  \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n2141|  \"identity_kind\": \"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n2142|  \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2143|  \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaad\",\n2144|  \"opaque_identity\": {},\n2145|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2146|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:45.000Z\",\n2147|  \"extensions\": {}\n2148|}\n2149|~~~\n2150|\n2151|### 5.6 Workspace Group Record\n2152|\n2153|The Workspace Group Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:workspace-group</code>\n2154|version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its closed top-level shape contains exactly\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
