{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5ff","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":346,"recorded_at":1780531400000687,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcb-c0ba-7312-9a08-212fe1851618"},"task_id":"01a0adcb-c0ba-7312-9a08-212fe1851618","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adcb-c0ba-7312-9a08-212fe1851618","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1470 line(s) above)\n1471|### 5.1 Session Record\n1472|\n1473|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1474|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1475|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1476|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1477|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1478|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1479|\n1480|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1481|| --- | --- | --- |\n1482|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1483|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1484|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1485|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1486|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Globally unique |\n1487|| <code>name</code> | string | Section 2.3 grammar |\n1488|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>direct</code> or <code>task_board</code> |\n1489|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic time |\n1490|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Allowlisted host at creation |\n1491|| <code>provider_id</code> | string | Lowercase plugin ID |\n1492|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Required |\n1493|| <code>execution_profile</code> | enum | <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code> |\n1494|| <code>launch_plan</code> | Launch Plan | Closed shape below; sanitized and secret-free |\n1495|| <code>task_board</code> | Task-board Reference or null | Required object exactly when <code>kind = task_board</code> |\n1496|| <code>fork_provenance</code> | Fork Provenance or null | Required object exactly when this record was created by fork |\n1497|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Required; may be empty; reverse-DNS keys only |\n1498|\n1499|The embedded Launch Plan is a closed object with exactly these members:\n1500|\n1501|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1502|| --- | --- | --- |\n1503|| <code>argv</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[1..128] | Each element is 1–4,096 UTF-8 bytes; total encoded argv is at most 65,536 bytes; never a shell command string |\n1504|| <code>cwd_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Names one workspace in the Session Record's workspace group |\n1505|| <code>cwd_relative</code> | string | <code>.</code> for the workspace root or a path satisfying Section 1.6 |\n1506|| <code>env_names</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[0..64] | Sorted, unique names matching <code>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}</code>; values resolve only from destination-local state |\n1507|| <code>env_literals</code> | map(environment-name,string)[0..64] | Non-secret literals of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes each; keys sorted in canonical form and disjoint from <code>env_names</code> |\n1508|| <code>contains_secrets</code> | boolean | MUST be false |\n1509|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1510|\n1511|Arguments MUST contain only sanitized provider/task-board arguments. Secret\n1512|values, inline credential-bearing URLs, response files containing secrets, and\n1513|shell fragments are forbidden. A name such as <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> in\n1514|<code>env_names</code> is a destination-local lookup instruction, not a stored\n1515|value.\n1516|\n1517|The Task-board Reference is a closed object:\n1518|\n1519|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1520|| --- | --- | --- |\n1521|| <code>bridge_protocol_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1522|| <code>board</code> | Board Identity | Closed shape below |\n1523|| <code>task_element_id</code> | string | 1–128 printable non-control UTF-8 bytes |\n1524|| <code>launch_mode</code> | enum | <code>primary_owner</code> or <code>tracked_prompt</code> |\n1525|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string or null | MUST be null in the immutable creation record; the public reference is established by <code>task_board.launched</code> and may later change through <code>task_board.adopted</code> |\n1526|| <code>board_goal</code> | Board Goal or null | Required non-null for <code>primary_owner</code> |\n1527|| <code>native_goal_binding</code> | enum | <code>bound</code>, <code>prompt</code>, or <code>none</code> |\n1528|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1529|\n1530|Board Identity has exactly <code>kind</code> (<code>local</code> or\n1531|<code>remote</code>), <code>logical_id</code> (1–128 characters matching\n1532|<code>[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}</code>),\n1533|<code>remote_url</code> (absolute <code>https</code> URL or null), and\n1534|<code>extensions</code>. A local board requires null <code>remote_url</code>;\n1535|a remote board requires a URL with no userinfo, query, or fragment. Board Goal\n1536|has exactly <code>schema = \"board-goal-v2\"</code>, <code>goal_id</code> as a\n1537|1–128 character public goal reference, <code>revision</code> as uint53 greater\n1538|than zero, and <code>extensions</code>. <code>primary_owner</code> requires\n1539|<code>native_goal_binding = bound</code>; <code>tracked_prompt</code> permits\n1540|<code>prompt</code> or <code>none</code> and MAY have a null goal.\n1541|\n1542|The creation-time <code>manager_session_ref</code> MUST be null for both launch\n1543|modes. This avoids making an immutable Session Record depend on a manager\n1544|reference that the public bridge has not created yet. The current reference is\n1545|the newest authoritative <code>task_board.launched</code> or\n1546|<code>task_board.adopted</code> event for the session; a missing event means the\n1547|task-board launch has not succeeded and MUST NOT be guessed from private state.\n1548|\n1549|Fork Provenance is a closed object with exactly\n1550|<code>source_session_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> digest,\n1551|<code>source_workspace_group_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>operation_id</code>\n1552|UUIDv7, <code>provider_fork_mode</code> as <code>native</code>,\n1553|<code>supported_import</code>, or <code>task_board_clone</code>, and\n1554|<code>extensions</code>. It is core provenance, not an extension, and MUST\n1555|remain immutable with the fork's Session Record.\n1556|\n1557|Normative example:\n1558|\n1559|~~~json\n1560|{\n1561|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1562|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1563|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:d61701066a7f5dd37bf35fea0e85e7f154251355ad24a49976532d7f79ddc772\",\n1564|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1565|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1566|  \"name\": \"payments-api\",\n1567|  \"kind\": \"direct\",\n1568|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:00:00.000Z\",\n1569|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1570|  \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n1571|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n1572|  \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n1573|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1574|    \"argv\": [\"codex\"],\n1575|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n1576|    \"cwd_relative\": \"src\",\n1577|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n1578|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1579|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1580|    \"extensions\": {}\n1581|  },\n1582|  \"task_board\": null,\n1583|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1584|  \"extensions\": {}\n1585|}\n1586|~~~\n1587|\n1588|A task-board Session Record uses the same Launch Plan shape and this exact\n1589|tagged variant:\n1590|\n1591|~~~json\n1592|{\n1593|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1594|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1595|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:0acd3e31635372e176f8f37b1b74aa0ebdcf2d1e4ac40d43adb8e462079b34a2\",\n1596|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1597|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1598|  \"name\": \"qwen-investigation\",\n1599|  \"kind\": \"task_board\",\n1600|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:01:00.000Z\",\n1601|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1602|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n1603|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-af70-7188-8172-1234567890ab\",\n1604|  \"execution_profile\": \"standard\",\n1605|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1606|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"qwen\", \"TASK-260819-example\"],\n1607|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\",\n1608|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n1609|    \"env_names\": [],\n1610|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1611|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1612|    \"extensions\": {}\n1613|  },\n1614|  \"task_board\": {\n1615|    \"bridge_protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1616|    \"board\": {\n1617|      \"kind\": \"local\",\n1618|      \"logical_id\": \"agent-session-manager-spec\",\n1619|      \"remote_url\": null,\n1620|      \"extensions\": {}\n1621|    },\n1622|    \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-example\",\n1623|    \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n1624|    \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n1625|    \"board_goal\": null,\n1626|    \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\",\n1627|    \"extensions\": {}\n1628|  },\n1629|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1630|  \"extensions\": {}\n1631|}\n1632|~~~\n1633|\n1634|The example <code>record_id</code>, like every self-identity digest in this\n1635|document, is the computed canonical digest. Validators MUST recompute it and\n1636|MUST reject a mismatch.\n1637|\n1638|Session Record 2.0.0 is emitted in v0.3.0 only for a cross-environment clone\n1639|target. It retains every major-1 field except <code>fork_provenance</code>,\n1640|which is replaced by required closed <code>derivation_provenance</code>.\n1641|Provider Protocol 2 launch/fork continues to emit and consume Session Record\n1642|1.0.0 with its exact nullable fork provenance; no in-place migration or silent\n1643|major retry is permitted.\n1644|\n1645|The derivation union has tags <code>origin</code>,\n1646|<code>same_provider_fork</code>, and <code>cross_environment_clone</code>.\n1647|The first two are reserved/read-only in v0.3 until a containing Provider\n1648|protocol adopts them. Cross-environment clone contains exactly:\n1649|\n1650|- <code>kind=cross_environment_clone</code>, operation UUIDv7, and bundle UUIDv7;\n1651|- <code>source_kind=ax_session|external_native</code>;\n1652|- nullable source Session Record, Checkpoint, and Provider Identity IDs, all\n1653|  non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>;\n1654|- a sanitized non-authoritative source native session ID;\n1655|- exact source and target Environment Tuples;\n1656|- source snapshot, Capture Manifest, Canonical Session, Projection Plan, and\n1657|  Migration Checkpoint digests;\n1658|- nullable previous Lineage Receipt and source profile Event IDs; and\n1659|- reverse-DNS extensions.\n1660|\n1661|The reserved <code>origin</code> variant contains exactly\n1662|<code>kind=origin</code>, <code>creation_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n1663|<code>extensions</code>. The reserved <code>same_provider_fork</code> variant\n1664|contains exactly <code>kind=same_provider_fork</code>,\n1665|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1666|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1667|<code>source_workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1668|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1669|<code>provider_fork_mode:native|supported_import|task_board_clone</code>,\n1670|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1671|\n1672|The <code>cross_environment_clone</code> variant's exact typed members are\n1673|<code>kind</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1674|<code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1675|<code>source_kind:ax_session|external_native</code>,\n1676|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n1677|<code>source_session_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1678|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest|null</code>,\n1679|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1680|<code>source_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n1681|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1682|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1683|<code>source_snapshot_digest:digest</code>,\n1684|<code>capture_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n1685|<code>canonical_session_id:digest</code>,\n1686|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n1687|<code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1688|<code>previous_lineage_receipt_id:digest|null</code>,\n1689|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1690|All four AX-source IDs are non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>.\n1691|\n1692|The new target Session ID and target <code>provider_id</code> are allocated at\n1693|creation and never reuse or mutate the source Session or source provider ID.\n1694|Target native identity, final reports, target Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt\n1695|are absent because they do not exist yet; Provider Identity and immutable clone\n1696|events bind those later facts without mutating the record or forming a digest\n1697|cycle. Task-board references remain orthogonal authority in the existing\n1698|<code>task_board</code> field; source goals, manager references, leases,\n1699|approvals, tokens, and pending operations do not transfer.\n1700|\n1701|Session Record 3.0.0 is the v0.4 creation contract. It retains every v2\n1702|top-level member and replaces the v2 derivation union with the closed creation\n1703|union <code>origin</code>, <code>same_provider_fork</code>,\n1704|<code>cross_environment_clone</code>, and <code>native_adoption</code>. The\n1705|first three retain their v2 exact shapes and semantics. The new\n1706|<code>native_adoption</code> variant contains exactly\n1707|<code>kind=native_adoption</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1708|<code>source_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_instance_id:digest</code>,\n1709|<code>source_observation_id:digest</code>,\n1710|<code>source_head_digest:digest</code>,\n1711|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1712|<code>target_provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n1713|and <code>extensions</code>. These are creation inputs only. Provider Identity,\n1714|first Checkpoint, adoption events, and Directory Operation Receipts are later\n1715|facts and MUST NOT appear in the creation record.\n1716|\n1717|Adoption creates a new Session ID around the existing native identity and does\n1718|not claim that pre-adoption history was AX-authored or fenced. Provider ID is\n1719|immutable after creation. Cross-environment move uses the existing\n1720|<code>cross_environment_clone</code> creation variant plus later Session Event\n1721|3/Directory Operation Receipt move lifecycle; it is not a fifth creation tag\n1722|and never rewrites the source Session.\n1723|\n1724|Session Record 1 and 2 remain readable and immutable. New origin/fork/clone/\n1725|adopt records written by a directory-capable v0.4 implementation use major 3;\n1726|no reader silently retries another major or translates an existing record in\n1727|place.\n1728|\n1729|### 5.2 Session Event\n1730|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c601","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":347,"recorded_at":1780531400000689,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcb-c0ba-7312-9a08-212fe1851618"},"task_id":"01a0adcb-c0ba-7312-9a08-212fe1851618","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0adcb-c0ba-7312-9a08-212fe1851618"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c603","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":348,"recorded_at":1780531400000691,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcbbc69714d8735c5cb343fce74","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1470 line(s) above)\n1471|### 5.1 Session Record\n1472|\n1473|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1474|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1475|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1476|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1477|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1478|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1479|\n1480|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1481|| --- | --- | --- |\n1482|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1483|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1484|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1485|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1486|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Globally unique |\n1487|| <code>name</code> | string | Section 2.3 grammar |\n1488|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>direct</code> or <code>task_board</code> |\n1489|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic time |\n1490|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Allowlisted host at creation |\n1491|| <code>provider_id</code> | string | Lowercase plugin ID |\n1492|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Required |\n1493|| <code>execution_profile</code> | enum | <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code> |\n1494|| <code>launch_plan</code> | Launch Plan | Closed shape below; sanitized and secret-free |\n1495|| <code>task_board</code> | Task-board Reference or null | Required object exactly when <code>kind = task_board</code> |\n1496|| <code>fork_provenance</code> | Fork Provenance or null | Required object exactly when this record was created by fork |\n1497|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Required; may be empty; reverse-DNS keys only |\n1498|\n1499|The embedded Launch Plan is a closed object with exactly these members:\n1500|\n1501|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1502|| --- | --- | --- |\n1503|| <code>argv</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[1..128] | Each element is 1–4,096 UTF-8 bytes; total encoded argv is at most 65,536 bytes; never a shell command string |\n1504|| <code>cwd_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Names one workspace in the Session Record's workspace group |\n1505|| <code>cwd_relative</code> | string | <code>.</code> for the workspace root or a path satisfying Section 1.6 |\n1506|| <code>env_names</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[0..64] | Sorted, unique names matching <code>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}</code>; values resolve only from destination-local state |\n1507|| <code>env_literals</code> | map(environment-name,string)[0..64] | Non-secret literals of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes each; keys sorted in canonical form and disjoint from <code>env_names</code> |\n1508|| <code>contains_secrets</code> | boolean | MUST be false |\n1509|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1510|\n1511|Arguments MUST contain only sanitized provider/task-board arguments. Secret\n1512|values, inline credential-bearing URLs, response files containing secrets, and\n1513|shell fragments are forbidden. A name such as <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> in\n1514|<code>env_names</code> is a destination-local lookup instruction, not a stored\n1515|value.\n1516|\n1517|The Task-board Reference is a closed object:\n1518|\n1519|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1520|| --- | --- | --- |\n1521|| <code>bridge_protocol_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1522|| <code>board</code> | Board Identity | Closed shape below |\n1523|| <code>task_element_id</code> | string | 1–128 printable non-control UTF-8 bytes |\n1524|| <code>launch_mode</code> | enum | <code>primary_owner</code> or <code>tracked_prompt</code> |\n1525|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string or null | MUST be null in the immutable creation record; the public reference is established by <code>task_board.launched</code> and may later change through <code>task_board.adopted</code> |\n1526|| <code>board_goal</code> | Board Goal or null | Required non-null for <code>primary_owner</code> |\n1527|| <code>native_goal_binding</code> | enum | <code>bound</code>, <code>prompt</code>, or <code>none</code> |\n1528|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1529|\n1530|Board Identity has exactly <code>kind</code> (<code>local</code> or\n1531|<code>remote</code>), <code>logical_id</code> (1–128 characters matching\n1532|<code>[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}</code>),\n1533|<code>remote_url</code> (absolute <code>https</code> URL or null), and\n1534|<code>extensions</code>. A local board requires null <code>remote_url</code>;\n1535|a remote board requires a URL with no userinfo, query, or fragment. Board Goal\n1536|has exactly <code>schema = \"board-goal-v2\"</code>, <code>goal_id</code> as a\n1537|1–128 character public goal reference, <code>revision</code> as uint53 greater\n1538|than zero, and <code>extensions</code>. <code>primary_owner</code> requires\n1539|<code>native_goal_binding = bound</code>; <code>tracked_prompt</code> permits\n1540|<code>prompt</code> or <code>none</code> and MAY have a null goal.\n1541|\n1542|The creation-time <code>manager_session_ref</code> MUST be null for both launch\n1543|modes. This avoids making an immutable Session Record depend on a manager\n1544|reference that the public bridge has not created yet. The current reference is\n1545|the newest authoritative <code>task_board.launched</code> or\n1546|<code>task_board.adopted</code> event for the session; a missing event means the\n1547|task-board launch has not succeeded and MUST NOT be guessed from private state.\n1548|\n1549|Fork Provenance is a closed object with exactly\n1550|<code>source_session_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> digest,\n1551|<code>source_workspace_group_id</code> UUIDv7, <code>operation_id</code>\n1552|UUIDv7, <code>provider_fork_mode</code> as <code>native</code>,\n1553|<code>supported_import</code>, or <code>task_board_clone</code>, and\n1554|<code>extensions</code>. It is core provenance, not an extension, and MUST\n1555|remain immutable with the fork's Session Record.\n1556|\n1557|Normative example:\n1558|\n1559|~~~json\n1560|{\n1561|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1562|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1563|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:d61701066a7f5dd37bf35fea0e85e7f154251355ad24a49976532d7f79ddc772\",\n1564|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1565|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1566|  \"name\": \"payments-api\",\n1567|  \"kind\": \"direct\",\n1568|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:00:00.000Z\",\n1569|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1570|  \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n1571|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n1572|  \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n1573|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1574|    \"argv\": [\"codex\"],\n1575|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n1576|    \"cwd_relative\": \"src\",\n1577|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n1578|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1579|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1580|    \"extensions\": {}\n1581|  },\n1582|  \"task_board\": null,\n1583|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1584|  \"extensions\": {}\n1585|}\n1586|~~~\n1587|\n1588|A task-board Session Record uses the same Launch Plan shape and this exact\n1589|tagged variant:\n1590|\n1591|~~~json\n1592|{\n1593|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-record\",\n1594|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1595|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:0acd3e31635372e176f8f37b1b74aa0ebdcf2d1e4ac40d43adb8e462079b34a2\",\n1596|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1597|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n1598|  \"name\": \"qwen-investigation\",\n1599|  \"kind\": \"task_board\",\n1600|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:01:00.000Z\",\n1601|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1602|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n1603|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-af70-7188-8172-1234567890ab\",\n1604|  \"execution_profile\": \"standard\",\n1605|  \"launch_plan\": {\n1606|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"qwen\", \"TASK-260819-example\"],\n1607|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\",\n1608|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n1609|    \"env_names\": [],\n1610|    \"env_literals\": {},\n1611|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n1612|    \"extensions\": {}\n1613|  },\n1614|  \"task_board\": {\n1615|    \"bridge_protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1616|    \"board\": {\n1617|      \"kind\": \"local\",\n1618|      \"logical_id\": \"agent-session-manager-spec\",\n1619|      \"remote_url\": null,\n1620|      \"extensions\": {}\n1621|    },\n1622|    \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-example\",\n1623|    \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n1624|    \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n1625|    \"board_goal\": null,\n1626|    \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\",\n1627|    \"extensions\": {}\n1628|  },\n1629|  \"fork_provenance\": null,\n1630|  \"extensions\": {}\n1631|}\n1632|~~~\n1633|\n1634|The example <code>record_id</code>, like every self-identity digest in this\n1635|document, is the computed canonical digest. Validators MUST recompute it and\n1636|MUST reject a mismatch.\n1637|\n1638|Session Record 2.0.0 is emitted in v0.3.0 only for a cross-environment clone\n1639|target. It retains every major-1 field except <code>fork_provenance</code>,\n1640|which is replaced by required closed <code>derivation_provenance</code>.\n1641|Provider Protocol 2 launch/fork continues to emit and consume Session Record\n1642|1.0.0 with its exact nullable fork provenance; no in-place migration or silent\n1643|major retry is permitted.\n1644|\n1645|The derivation union has tags <code>origin</code>,\n1646|<code>same_provider_fork</code>, and <code>cross_environment_clone</code>.\n1647|The first two are reserved/read-only in v0.3 until a containing Provider\n1648|protocol adopts them. Cross-environment clone contains exactly:\n1649|\n1650|- <code>kind=cross_environment_clone</code>, operation UUIDv7, and bundle UUIDv7;\n1651|- <code>source_kind=ax_session|external_native</code>;\n1652|- nullable source Session Record, Checkpoint, and Provider Identity IDs, all\n1653|  non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>;\n1654|- a sanitized non-authoritative source native session ID;\n1655|- exact source and target Environment Tuples;\n1656|- source snapshot, Capture Manifest, Canonical Session, Projection Plan, and\n1657|  Migration Checkpoint digests;\n1658|- nullable previous Lineage Receipt and source profile Event IDs; and\n1659|- reverse-DNS extensions.\n1660|\n1661|The reserved <code>origin</code> variant contains exactly\n1662|<code>kind=origin</code>, <code>creation_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n1663|<code>extensions</code>. The reserved <code>same_provider_fork</code> variant\n1664|contains exactly <code>kind=same_provider_fork</code>,\n1665|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1666|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1667|<code>source_workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1668|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1669|<code>provider_fork_mode:native|supported_import|task_board_clone</code>,\n1670|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1671|\n1672|The <code>cross_environment_clone</code> variant's exact typed members are\n1673|<code>kind</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1674|<code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1675|<code>source_kind:ax_session|external_native</code>,\n1676|<code>source_session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n1677|<code>source_session_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1678|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest|null</code>,\n1679|<code>source_provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n1680|<code>source_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n1681|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1682|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1683|<code>source_snapshot_digest:digest</code>,\n1684|<code>capture_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n1685|<code>canonical_session_id:digest</code>,\n1686|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n1687|<code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n1688|<code>previous_lineage_receipt_id:digest|null</code>,\n1689|<code>source_profile_event_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n1690|All four AX-source IDs are non-null exactly for <code>ax_session</code>.\n1691|\n1692|The new target Session ID and target <code>provider_id</code> are allocated at\n1693|creation and never reuse or mutate the source Session or source provider ID.\n1694|Target native identity, final reports, target Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt\n1695|are absent because they do not exist yet; Provider Identity and immutable clone\n1696|events bind those later facts without mutating the record or forming a digest\n1697|cycle. Task-board references remain orthogonal authority in the existing\n1698|<code>task_board</code> field; source goals, manager references, leases,\n1699|approvals, tokens, and pending operations do not transfer.\n1700|\n1701|Session Record 3.0.0 is the v0.4 creation contract. It retains every v2\n1702|top-level member and replaces the v2 derivation union with the closed creation\n1703|union <code>origin</code>, <code>same_provider_fork</code>,\n1704|<code>cross_environment_clone</code>, and <code>native_adoption</code>. The\n1705|first three retain their v2 exact shapes and semantics. The new\n1706|<code>native_adoption</code> variant contains exactly\n1707|<code>kind=native_adoption</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1708|<code>source_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_instance_id:digest</code>,\n1709|<code>source_observation_id:digest</code>,\n1710|<code>source_head_digest:digest</code>,\n1711|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n1712|<code>target_provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n1713|and <code>extensions</code>. These are creation inputs only. Provider Identity,\n1714|first Checkpoint, adoption events, and Directory Operation Receipts are later\n1715|facts and MUST NOT appear in the creation record.\n1716|\n1717|Adoption creates a new Session ID around the existing native identity and does\n1718|not claim that pre-adoption history was AX-authored or fenced. Provider ID is\n1719|immutable after creation. Cross-environment move uses the existing\n1720|<code>cross_environment_clone</code> creation variant plus later Session Event\n1721|3/Directory Operation Receipt move lifecycle; it is not a fifth creation tag\n1722|and never rewrites the source Session.\n1723|\n1724|Session Record 1 and 2 remain readable and immutable. New origin/fork/clone/\n1725|adopt records written by a directory-capable v0.4 implementation use major 3;\n1726|no reader silently retries another major or translates an existing record in\n1727|place.\n1728|\n1729|### 5.2 Session Event\n1730|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
