n, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\\n3149:| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\\n3150:| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\\n3421:    \\\"execution_profile\\\": \\\"yolo\\\",\\n3455:    \\\"profile_mapping\\\": \\\"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\\\",\\n3502:| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \\\"default_unrestricted_tool_set\\\"</code> |\\n3832:contradiction is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\\n4270:A mismatch is <code>integrity_failure</code>. <code>ax</code> MUST NOT synthesize\\n4367:  \\\"execution_profile\\\": \\\"yolo\\\",\\n4368:  \\\"profile_source_event_id\\\": null,\\n4442:provider-ID grammar; <code>execution_profile</code> is\\n4443:<code>standard|yolo</code>; <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is a digest or\\n4466:| <code>execution_profile</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id</code> | Copy the Section 2.4 effective profile and nullable source at the exported checkpoint; null requires equality with the Session Record creation profile, while non-null MUST name the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event reachable from that checkpoint's event heads |\\n4513:  \\\"execution_profile\\\": \\\"standard\\\",\\n4514:  \\\"profile_source_event_id\\\": null,\\n4560:<code>execution_profile = standard</code>, applies an authoritative\\n4561:<code>profile.changed</code> event to <code>yolo</code>, and exports a checkpoint\\n4563:<code>execution_profile = yolo</code> and that event's digest in\\n4564:<code>profile_source_event_id</code>. <code>TB-BUNDLE-PROFILE-N1</code> copies\\n5258:| <code>TM-ENTRY-FILE-N1</code> | Descriptor size differs from file size | <code>integrity_failure</code> |\\n5264:| <code>TM-GIT-N4</code> | Working-tree manifest or project config is outside child closure | <code>integrity_failure</code> |\\n5266:| <code>TM-GIT-N6</code> | <code>gitlink_oid</code> differs from the parent stage-0 mode-160000 index entry | <code>integrity_failure</code> |\\n5921:| <code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code> | Plugin says committed but destination marker/plan differs | <code>integrity_failure</code>; quarantine transaction and mutate nothing further |\\n6102:| Marker digest, path fingerprint, predecessor chain, or referenced object is invalid | <code>integrity_failure</code>; report managed divergence diagnostically and mutate nothing |\\n6234:| C claims deletion/resurrection without the required ancestry, or the entry digest differs from the resolution event | <code>integrity_failure</code>; retain staging and both histories. |\\n7385:| <code>materialize.finalize</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,rollback_token:base64url-256+,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation,activation:dormant_validated&#124;direct_owner_resumed&#124;task_board_owner_resumed,execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo&#124;null,profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null}</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,phase:committed,committed_checkpoint_id:digest,managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,destination_marker_id:digest&#124;null,provider_transaction_state:none&#124;committed,task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;resumed&#124;dormant_finalized,manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null,finalized_at:timestamp}</code> |\\n7439:<code>fork.created.source_profile_event_id</code>.\\n7921:<code>integrity_failure</code>.\\n7995:is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\\n9023:   <code>execution_profile</code> equal to the Session Record and\\n9024:   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>.\\n9122:   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>; this event, not an edit to the Session\\n9594:   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>, the source checkpoint's nullable\\n9595:   profile event in <code>source_profile_event_id</code>, and mode; then record\\n9754:  \\\"execution_profile\\\": \\\"yolo\\\",\\n10870:read is <code>integrity_failure</code>, never absence and never a trigger for an\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 17281,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4321,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c677","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":406,"recorded_at":1780531400000807,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcb-e390-7742-91e8-a4e514b21bd6"},"task_id":"01a0adcb-e390-7742-91e8-a4e514b21bd6","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0adcb-e390-7742-91e8-a4e514b21bd6"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c679","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":407,"recorded_at":1780531400000809,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcbdcc47313a324ed26da3017c4","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1982 line(s) above)\n1983|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n1984|\n1985|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n1986|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n1987|\n1988|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1989|| --- | --- | --- |\n1990|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n1991|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1992|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1993|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1994|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n1995|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n1996|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n1997|| <code>safe_boundary</code> | Safe Boundary Evidence | Closed shape below |\n1998|| <code>event_heads</code> | sorted unique digest[1..64] | Authoritative event DAG heads immediately before this object |\n1999|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Workspace-group Transfer Manifest root |\n2000|| <code>provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null | Direct native-store/provider snapshot only |\n2001|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Task-board path only |\n2002|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Current lease holder |\n2003|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2004|| <code>status</code> | enum | Literal <code>validated</code> |\n2005|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2006|\n2007|Safe Boundary Evidence is a closed object containing exactly\n2008|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n2009|<code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>,\n2010|<code>evidence:provider_api|provider_event|managed_pty|task_board_bridge|accepted_test</code>,\n2011|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n2012|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, and\n2013|<code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>. A published checkpoint requires all\n2014|three booleans true and both counters zero. Provider-specific scheduled or\n2015|child work is included in <code>background_idle</code> and\n2016|<code>open_processes</code>; an adapter that cannot prove it MUST NOT publish a\n2017|new checkpoint.\n2018|\n2019|The referenced Session Record selects the persistence variant. For\n2020|<code>kind = direct</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be non-null\n2021|and <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be null. A backend-resolved provider\n2022|with no portable bytes still uses a provider Transfer Manifest containing its\n2023|validated identity and zero file entries; null is not used to erase that\n2024|distinction. For <code>kind = task_board</code>,\n2025|<code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be null and\n2026|<code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be non-null. Both-null and both-non-null\n2027|checkpoints are invalid.\n2028|\n2029|A checkpoint MUST NOT be published until every referenced object exists,\n2030|hashes correctly, passes schema validation, and the provider/task-board path\n2031|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2032|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2033|\n2034|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2035|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2036|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2037|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2038|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2039|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2040|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2041|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2042|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2043|\n2044|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2045|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2046|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2047|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2048|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2049|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2050|\n2051|Normative example:\n2052|\n2053|~~~json\n2054|{\n2055|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2056|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2057|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2058|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2059|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2060|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n2061|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2062|  \"safe_boundary\": {\n2063|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n2064|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n2065|    \"evidence\": \"accepted_test\",\n2066|    \"input_blocked\": true,\n2067|    \"foreground_idle\": true,\n2068|    \"background_idle\": true,\n2069|    \"open_processes\": 0,\n2070|    \"open_database_handles\": 0\n2071|  },\n2072|  \"event_heads\": [\n2073|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n2074|  ],\n2075|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n2076|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2077|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2078|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2079|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2080|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2081|  \"extensions\": {}\n2082|}\n2083|~~~\n2084|\n2085|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2086|\n2087|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":408,"recorded_at":1780531400000811,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcbdef1719097d8a35c098e2848","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-11-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n 'set-profile\\\\|profile_mapping_unavailable\\\\|integrity_failure\\\\|profile\\\\.changed\\\\|execution_profile\\\\|profile_source_event_id\\\\|source_profile_event_id\\\\|profile_mapping' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -80\",\n  \"description\": \"Find profile-related spec references\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"637:<code>profile.changed</code> event from which it was derived, or null when the\\n639:<code>ax session set-profile NAME PROFILE</code>, a new event under the current\\n641:MUST fail with <code>profile_mapping_unavailable</code> if the adapter cannot\\n645:newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in lease/sequence order.\\n655:session's <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null. The\\n656:<code>fork.created.source_profile_event_id</code> separately preserves the\\n666:Record profile, E1 an authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event to P1,\\n673:| <code>PROFILE-DIRECT-FORK</code> | Fork C1 | New Session Record creation profile is P1; fork event carries P1/null as new-session authority plus <code>source_profile_event_id=E1</code>; resumed carries P1/null |\\n676:| <code>PROFILE-TB-FORK</code> | Task-board fork C1 | Source bundle carries P1/E1; new Session Record and bridge resume use P1/null; fork event retains E1 only in <code>source_profile_event_id</code> |\\n681:<code>int