{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6bd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":441,"recorded_at":1780531400000877,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcbefd6724f8120d7ded3828f1c","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(4339 line(s) above)\n4340|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. If an adopt response is lost,\n4341|<code>status</code> is the only recovery read: an exact <code>ax_binding</code>\n4342|proves adoption, null proves dormancy, and a different binding is\n4343|<code>lease_conflict</code>. Expired unadopted dormant state MAY be garbage\n4344|collected after its immutable bundle remains available; it MUST never start a\n4345|provider.\n4346|\n4347|Replica sync normally ends after import/open. Graceful takeover performs adopt\n4348|only after the destination lease wins. A failed adopt MUST leave the old owner\n4349|unchanged in a graceful flow and the destination dormant. A pre-stop aborted\n4350|handoff uses <code>resume</code> under the still-winning source lease to release\n4351|input; no private manager mutation is permitted.\n4352|\n4353|### 9.3 Task-board Bundle\n4354|\n4355|The portable archive has schema <code>urn:ax:schema:task-board-bundle</code>\n4356|version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its public <code>bundle.json</code> contains:\n4357|\n4358|~~~json\n4359|{\n4360|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:task-board-bundle\",\n4361|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4362|  \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n4363|  \"manager_contract\": \"tb-session-bundle-v1\",\n4364|  \"bridge_protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4365|  \"logical_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n4366|  \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n4367|  \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n4368|  \"profile_source_event_id\": null,\n4369|  \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-example\",\n4370|  \"launch_mode\": \"primary_owner\",\n4371|  \"provider_snapshot\": {\n4372|    \"media_type\": \"application/vnd.task-board.session+opaque\",\n4373|    \"blob_id\": \"sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\"\n4374|  },\n4375|  \"manager_record\": {\n4376|    \"blob_id\": \"sha256:dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd\"\n4377|  },\n4378|  \"sanitized_launch_plan\": {\n4379|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"codex\", \"TASK-260819-example\"],\n4380|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n4381|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n4382|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n4383|    \"env_literals\": {\n4384|      \"AX_TASK_MODE\": \"primary\"\n4385|    },\n4386|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n4387|    \"extensions\": {\n4388|      \"works.relux.ax.launch-hint\": {\n4389|        \"source\": \"task-board\"\n4390|      }\n4391|    }\n4392|  },\n4393|  \"source_owner_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n4394|  \"board_goal\": {\n4395|    \"schema\": \"board-goal-v2\",\n4396|    \"goal_id\": \"PRIMARY-GOAL-260819-example\",\n4397|    \"revision\": 3,\n4398|    \"extensions\": {\n4399|      \"works.relux.ax.goal-label\": \"spec-release\"\n4400|    }\n4401|  },\n4402|  \"native_goal_binding\": {\n4403|    \"state\": \"bound\",\n4404|    \"opaque_blob_id\": \"sha256:eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\"\n4405|  },\n4406|  \"board_identity\": {\n4407|    \"kind\": \"local\",\n4408|    \"logical_id\": \"board-0198f4c8\",\n4409|    \"remote_url\": null,\n4410|    \"extensions\": {\n4411|      \"works.relux.ax.board-scope\": \"specification\"\n4412|    }\n4413|  },\n4414|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n4415|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:10:00.000Z\"\n4416|}\n4417|~~~\n4418|\n4419|The bundle object is closed and every displayed top-level member is required.\n4420|Its nested objects are also closed:\n4421|\n4422|- <code>provider_snapshot</code> contains exactly\n4423|  <code>media_type = application/vnd.task-board.session+opaque</code> and\n4424|  <code>blob_id:digest</code>;\n4425|- <code>manager_record</code> contains exactly <code>blob_id:digest</code>;\n4426|- <code>sanitized_launch_plan</code> is the complete closed Section 5.1 Launch\n4427|  Plan, including cwd, non-secret literal environment, and extensions; its\n4428|  <code>contains_secrets</code> member is false;\n4429|- <code>board_goal</code> is null or is the complete closed Section 5.1 Board\n4430|  Goal, including <code>extensions</code>;\n4431|- <code>native_goal_binding</code> contains exactly\n4432|  <code>state:bound|prompt|none</code> and\n4433|  <code>opaque_blob_id:digest|null</code>, with non-null required only for\n4434|  <code>bound</code>; and\n4435|- <code>board_identity</code> is the complete closed Section 5.1 Board Identity,\n4436|  including <code>extensions</code> and its local/remote URL rule.\n4437|\n4438|<code>manager_contract</code> is the literal\n4439|<code>tb-session-bundle-v1</code> and\n4440|<code>bridge_protocol_version</code> is exactly <code>1.0.0</code>. Logical\n4441|session and workspace group IDs are UUIDv7; <code>provider_id</code> uses the\n4442|provider-ID grammar; <code>execution_profile</code> is\n4443|<code>standard|yolo</code>; <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is a digest or\n4444|null; <code>task_element_id</code> has the Section 5.1\n4445|1–128 printable non-control UTF-8 constraint; source owner is UUIDv7;\n4446|<code>launch_mode</code> is <code>primary_owner|tracked_prompt</code>; and\n4447|<code>created_at</code> is diagnostic UTC time.\n4448|\n4449|The bundle MUST carry the durable manager record, provider snapshot, sanitized\n4450|launch plan with no secret values, source owner identity, native goal-binding\n4451|state, and logical board/workspace identities. A\n4452|<code>launch_mode = primary_owner</code> requires a non-null exact\n4453|<code>board-goal-v2</code> reference/revision and\n4454|<code>native_goal_binding.state = bound</code>. A\n4455|<code>launch_mode = tracked_prompt</code> MAY have <code>board_goal = null</code>; when\n4456|null, binding state MUST be <code>prompt</code> or <code>none</code> and its blob\n4457|ID MUST be null.\n4458|\n4459|Export uses this exact projection; no exporter-specific omission or\n4460|normalization is permitted:\n4461|\n4462|| Bundle member | Authoritative source and equality rule |\n4463|| --- | --- |\n4464|| <code>bridge_protocol_version</code> | Whole-value equality with <code>SessionRecord.task_board.bridge_protocol_version</code> and the active bridge protocol |\n4465|| <code>logical_session_id</code>, <code>provider_id</code>, <code>workspace_group_id</code> | Copy the equal Session Record members exactly |\n4466|| <code>execution_profile</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id</code> | Copy the Section 2.4 effective profile and nullable source at the exported checkpoint; null requires equality with the Session Record creation profile, while non-null MUST name the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event reachable from that checkpoint's event heads |\n4467|| <code>task_element_id</code>, <code>launch_mode</code> | Copy <code>SessionRecord.task_board.task_element_id</code> and <code>.launch_mode</code> exactly |\n4468|| <code>sanitized_launch_plan</code> | Whole-object JCS equality with <code>SessionRecord.launch_plan</code>; preserve cwd, every non-secret literal, and every allowed extension with identical canonical JCS bytes |\n4469|| <code>board_identity</code>, <code>board_goal</code> | Whole-object JCS equality with <code>SessionRecord.task_board.board</code> and <code>.board_goal</code>, including all extension maps and null |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6bf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":442,"recorded_at":1780531400000879,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcbf24f7069bb1c3a325aeffa77","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(2941 line(s) above)\n2942|### 7.5 Required operations\n2943|\n2944|All plugins MUST implement every operation and return\n2945|<code>capability_unavailable</code> when the provider lacks the surface.\n2946|\n2947|Every request and success <code>body</code> is a closed object. The following\n2948|embedded types are part of provider protocol 2.0.0:\n2949|\n2950|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n2951|| --- | --- |\n2952|| <code>LeaseToken</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53 &gt; 0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n2953|| <code>WorkspacePaths</code> | <code>map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]</code>; paths are destination-native, canonical, and contain no NUL |\n2954|| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\n2955|| <code>ProcessObservation</code> | <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>executable_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>started_at:timestamp</code>, <code>candidate_store_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..256]</code>, <code>candidate_native_ids:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>; no PID is carried |\n2956|| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\n2957|| <code>SafeBoundaryProof</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean&#124;null</code>, <code>open_child_count:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handle_count:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique enum[0..5]</code> |\n2958|| <code>ValidationEvidence</code> | <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>status:passed&#124;skipped</code>, <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code> |\n2959|| <code>NativeDiscoveryProof</code> | <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>discovered:boolean</code>, <code>discovery_root:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>backend_resolved:boolean</code> |\n2960|| <code>ProcessClosure</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n2961|| <code>DoctorFinding</code> | <code>severity:info&#124;warning&#124;error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>, <code>remediation:string[1..4096]&#124;null</code>, <code>evidence:documented&#124;probed&#124;accepted_test&#124;provider_contract&#124;inferred&#124;acceptance_required&#124;none</code> |\n2962|| <code>ProviderStoreAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>access:capture_source&#124;materialize_destination</code> |\n2963|| <code>AuthorityTarget</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>relative_path:.&#124;path</code> |\n2964|| <code>ProviderCaptureItem</code> | <code>source_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>source_relative_path:path</code>, <code>manifest_path:path</code>, <code>kind:file&#124;directory</code>, <code>state_class:durable_payload&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>required:boolean</code> |\n2965|| <code>ProviderCapturePlan</code> | <code>capture_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_authorities:ProviderStoreAuthority[1..32]</code>, <code>items:ProviderCaptureItem[1..32768]</code>, <code>excluded_targets:AuthorityTarget[0..4096]</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]</code>, <code>snapshot_requires_closed_store:boolean</code> |\n2966|| <code>ObjectSink</code> | <code>root:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>create_mode:exclusive</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2967|| <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_objects</code>, <code>kind:provider_object_source</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>access:read_only</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2968|| <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>kind:provider_transaction</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:provider_transaction_v1</code>, <code>access:read_write</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids:sorted unique root-id[1..32]</code> |\n2969|| <code>ProviderTransactionEntry</code> | <code>sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>provider_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>target_relative_path:path</code>, <code>expected_prior_digest:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>prior_kind:absent&#124;file&#124;directory&#124;symlink&#124;hardlink</code>, <code>backup_relative_path:path&#124;null</code>, <code>applied:boolean</code>, <code>restored:boolean</code> |\n2970|| <code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code> | <code>protocol:urn:ax:protocol:provider</code>, <code>protocol_version:2.0.0</code>, <code>document_kind:materialization_transaction</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>state:preparing&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;committed&#124;rolling_back&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>entries:ProviderTransactionEntry[1..65536]</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, <code>updated_at:timestamp</code>, <code>terminal_at:timestamp&#124;null</code> |\n2971|| <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>state:unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code> |\n2972|\n2973|The <code>SafeBoundaryProof.blockers</code> enum is\n2974|<code>background_unproven</code>, <code>child_process_open</code>,\n2975|<code>database_handle_open</code>, <code>provider_busy</code>, or\n2976|<code>store_unstable</code>. A safe proof requires empty blockers,\n2977|<code>input_blocked</code>, <code>foreground_idle</code>,\n2978|<code>background_idle = true</code>, both counts zero, and non-null boundary and\n2979|store generation. <code>ValidationEvidence</code> arrays MUST be sorted by\n2980|<code>code</code> with no duplicate code. Opaque process handles are valid only\n2981|for the operation lifetime and MUST NOT be persisted or replicated.\n2982|\n2983|The <code>root-id</code> grammar is\n2984|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code>. Capture authorities are sorted by\n2985|<code>authority_id</code>, have <code>access = capture_source</code>, and are\n2986|unique. Capture items are sorted by <code>manifest_path</code>; each authority\n2987|reference MUST resolve, and\n2988|<code>root_path/source_relative_path</code> MUST remain under that exact root\n2989|after symlink/reparse-point resolution. Items MUST neither overlap nor traverse\n2990|through a symlink. Excluded targets are sorted by authority ID then relative\n2991|path and MUST reference the same authority set. <code>derived_cache</code> is\n2992|included only when Section 8 identifies it as required discovery metadata;\n2993|otherwise it must be excluded. Provider roots that contain credentials,\n2994|machine authentication, runtime sockets, locks, or live ax state MUST be\n2995|rejected even when a plugin names them. <code>ObjectSink.root</code> is a fresh owner-only directory\n2996|created by <code>ax</code>. Under <code>sha256_loose_v1</code>, a plugin writes\n2997|each complete blob with create-new semantics at\n2998|the exact Section 3.2 <code>digest_path_v1</code> relative path\n2999|<code>sha256/HH/REST</code> (two-hex shard, 62-hex leaf).\n3000|It MUST NOT create symlinks, hardlinks, devices, sockets, or any file not named\n3001|by its returned descriptors. The host independently hashes every sink file,\n3002|checks size/limits/exclusions, and only then imports it into the ax object\n3003|store. A plugin never receives the live object-store root.\n3004|\n3005|The destination host, not the peer and not the plugin, constructs both\n3006|materialization authorities. A <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority.root_path</code>\n3007|MUST equal\n3008|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-object-sources/&lt;materialization-id&gt;/&lt;provider-id&gt;</code>;\n3009|it is a fresh owner-only directory containing exactly the verified manifest\n3010|closure at the same <code>digest_path_v1</code> paths. The host makes every file read-only\n3011|before invoking the plugin. The authority's manifest IDs, byte/blob limits,\n3012|materialization ID, and provider ID MUST equal the selected checkpoint and\n3013|plan. An extra file, writable file, symlink, digest mismatch, or path supplied\n3014|by a remote request is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n3015|\n3016|A <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path</code> MUST equal\n3017|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-transactions/&lt;provider-id&gt;/&lt;transaction-id&gt;</code>.\n3018|It is a fresh owner-only directory, is disjoint from the object source and all\n3019|plan roots, and names exactly the materialization/provider/transaction/plan in\n3020|the authority. Its\n3021|<code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids</code> MUST equal the sorted set of\n3022|all <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority IDs used by plan operations. The\n3023|host MUST prove that the transaction root and every named provider-store root\n3024|are on the same filesystem/volume before the first plugin mutation. If one is\n3025|not, provider protocol 2.0.0 fails with <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>; it MUST\n3026|NOT fall back to an in-place cross-filesystem copy.\n3027|\n3028|The <code>provider_transaction_v1</code> layout contains only these durable\n3029|paths, plus one same-directory temporary file while atomically replacing\n3030|<code>transaction.json</code>:\n3031|\n3032|~~~text\n3033|transaction.json\n3034|staged/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n3035|backups/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n3036|~~~\n3037|\n3038|<code>transaction.json</code> is the UTF-8 JCS encoding of the closed\n3039|<code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code>. Entries are sorted by sequence and\n3040|are exactly the provider-store operations in the plan. For a pre-existing\n3041|target, <code>backup_relative_path</code> is exactly\n3042|<code>backups/&lt;provider-authority-id&gt;/&lt;operation-sequence&gt;</code>; an absent\n3043|target requires <code>prior_kind = absent</code>, a null backup path, and a null\n3044|expected prior digest. Every other prior kind requires that exact non-null\n3045|backup path and a non-null expected prior digest. A prepared document has every\n3046|entry applied, no entry restored, a non-null rollback token, and non-null native\n3047|discovery. A committed document keeps the applied facts, sets the token to\n3048|null, removes every staged/backup payload from disk, and has non-null\n3049|discovery. A rolled-\n3050|back document has every pre-existing entry restored, every transaction-created\n3051|target removed, a null token, and discovery describing the restored\n3052|destination. The plugin MUST fsync a staged replacement and the\n3053|transaction document, atomically rename any predecessor into its backup, then\n3054|atomically rename the staged replacement into the exact target. Each document\n3055|transition is written to a fresh temporary regular file, fsynced, renamed over\n3056|<code>transaction.json</code>, and followed by a parent-directory fsync where\n3057|the platform supports it. Windows uses replace/write-through semantics with\n3058|equivalent user-only DACLs.\n3059|\n3060|<code>terminal_at</code> is null in <code>preparing</code>,\n3061|<code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, and\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
