{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":467,"recorded_at":1780531400000929,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcc-0556-7f83-b1b2-cae26b6e41f6"},"task_id":"01a0adcc-0556-7f83-b1b2-cae26b6e41f6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adcc-0556-7f83-b1b2-cae26b6e41f6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3379 line(s) above)\n3380|\n3381|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\n3382|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\n3383|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\n3384|<code>lease_lost</code>, <code>validation_failed</code>,\n3385|<code>resume_failed</code>, <code>operator_abort</code>, and\n3386|<code>crash_recovery</code>. Each reason is persisted before restoration and\n3387|replaying the same request returns the same terminal result; changing only the\n3388|reason is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3389|\n3390|Normative <code>resume</code> request body and success body:\n3391|\n3392|~~~json\n3393|{\n3394|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3395|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3396|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3397|  \"operation\": \"resume\",\n3398|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:20:00.000Z\",\n3399|  \"body\": {\n3400|    \"identity\": {\n3401|      \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3402|      \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3403|      \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3404|      \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3405|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3406|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3407|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3408|      \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3409|      \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3410|      \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3411|      \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3412|      \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3413|      \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3414|      \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3415|      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3416|      \"extensions\": {}\n3417|    },\n3418|    \"workspace_paths\": {\n3419|      \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api\"\n3420|    },\n3421|    \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n3422|    \"terminal\": {\n3423|      \"backend\": \"tmux\",\n3424|      \"terminal_id\": \"ax-payments-api\",\n3425|      \"interactive\": true,\n3426|      \"columns\": 120,\n3427|      \"rows\": 40\n3428|    },\n3429|    \"lease\": {\n3430|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3431|      \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n3432|      \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3433|    }\n3434|  }\n3435|}\n3436|~~~\n3437|\n3438|~~~json\n3439|{\n3440|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3441|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3442|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3443|  \"ok\": true,\n3444|  \"body\": {\n3445|    \"argv\": [\n3446|      \"codex\",\n3447|      \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3448|      \"resume\",\n3449|      \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"\n3450|    ],\n3451|    \"cwd\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api/src\",\n3452|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n3453|    \"env_literals\": {},\n3454|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3455|    \"profile_mapping\": \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3456|    \"extensions\": {}\n3457|  }\n3458|}\n3459|~~~\n3460|\n3461|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3462|\n3463|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n3464|\n3465|- provider ID and exact version;\n3466|- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\n3467|- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\n3468|- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\n3469|- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\n3470|- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\n3471|- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\n3472|- <code>safe = true</code>.\n3473|\n3474|If background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\n3475|<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\n3476|takeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\n3477|request.\n3478|\n3479|For a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\n3480|provider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\n3481|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\n3482|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n3483|<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\n3484|adapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\n3485|<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\n3486|<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\n3487|generation, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\n3488|<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\n3489|provider-defined mapping is permitted.\n3490|\n3491|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3492|\n3493|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3494|\n3495|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3496|| --- | --- |\n3497|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3498|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3499|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
