horizes adding them.\n4483|\n4484|The projection above is exhaustive rather than implicitly lossy. The Session\n4485|Record's schema/version, record/subject identity, name, creation facts,\n4486|<code>kind = task_board</code>, creation-time execution profile, fork\n4487|provenance, and record-level extensions\n4488|remain in the separately replicated Session Record and MUST NOT be duplicated\n4489|inside the bundle. Within its Task-board Reference,\n4490|<code>bridge_protocol_version</code>, board, task element, launch mode, goal,\n4491|and native-binding enum are projected exactly as stated above. The creation-time\n4492|<code>manager_session_ref = null</code> is not serialized: the newest\n4493|authoritative launch/adoption event selects the public manager reference used\n4494|for this export. Task-board-Reference-level extensions remain ax metadata in\n4495|the Session Record because bridge protocol 1.0.0 has no corresponding field;\n4496|they MUST NOT be inserted into another bundle object or discarded from the\n4497|replicated Session Record. Likewise, bridge request operation/lease/workspace\n4498|paths and bridge result process/capability facts are operation-local; the\n4499|authoritative Session Event and Checkpoint retain the durable facts required by\n4500|their schemas. An exporter or importer MUST apply these inclusion/exclusion\n4501|rules exactly and MUST reject an attempt to tunnel an excluded field through a\n4502|different extension map.\n4503|\n4504|The complete example above is\n4505|<code>TB-BUNDLE-PROJECTION-PRIMARY-POS</code>: its source Session Record and\n4506|bridge launch request contain the displayed non-secret literal and all three\n4507|displayed extension maps, and export/import MUST reproduce them exactly. The\n4508|normative <code>TB-BUNDLE-PROMPT-POS</code> variant replaces the corresponding\n4509|members with this exact projected data and recomputes <code>bundle_id</code>:\n4510|\n4511|~~~json\n4512|{\n4513|  \"execution_profile\": \"standard\",\n4514|  \"profile_source_event_id\": null,\n4515|  \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-prompt-example\",\n4516|  \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n4517|  \"sanitized_launch_plan\": {\n4518|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"qwen\", \"TASK-260819-prompt-example\"],\n4519|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\",\n4520|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n4521|    \"env_names\": [],\n4522|    \"env_literals\": {\n4523|      \"AX_TASK_MODE\": \"prompt\"\n4524|    },\n4525|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n4526|    \"extensions\": {\n4527|      \"works.relux.ax.launch-hint\": {\n4528|        \"source\": \"tracked-prompt\"\n4529|      }\n4530|    }\n4531|  },\n4532|  \"board_goal\": null,\n4533|  \"native_goal_binding\": {\n4534|    \"state\": \"prompt\",\n4535|    \"opaque_blob_id\": null\n4536|  },\n4537|  \"board_identity\": {\n4538|    \"kind\": \"local\",\n4539|    \"logical_id\": \"agent-session-manager-spec\",\n4540|    \"remote_url\": null,\n4541|    \"extensions\": {\n4542|      \"works.relux.ax.board-scope\": \"prompt-research\"\n4543|    }\n4544|  }\n4545|}\n4546|~~~\n4547|\n4548|<code>TB-BUNDLE-PROMPT-N1</code> changes only the binding state to\n4549|<code>bound</code>, <code>TB-BUNDLE-PROMPT-N2</code> adds a non-null opaque blob,\n4550|and <code>TB-BUNDLE-PRIMARY-N1</code> changes the primary example goal to null.\n4551|All three MUST be rejected; prompt mode is never made unexportable merely\n4552|because it lacks a goal.\n4553|<code>TB-BUNDLE-PROJECTION-N1</code> drops the launch literal,\n4554|<code>TB-BUNDLE-PROJECTION-N2</code> drops one Board/Goal/Launch extension, and\n4555|<code>TB-BUNDLE-PROJECTION-N3</code> changes cwd while retaining a valid\n4556|standalone Launch Plan. Each fails projected equality before bridge import;\n4557|importers MUST NOT silently fill or strip the value.\n4558|\n4559|<code>TB-BUNDLE-PROFILE-CHANGED-POS</code> starts from a Session Record with\n4560|<code>execution_profile = standard</code>, applies an authoritative\n4561|<code>profile.changed</code> event to <code>yolo</code>, and exports a checkpoint\n4562|whose closure contains that event. Its bundle MUST carry\n4563|<code>execution_profile = yolo</code> and that event's digest in\n4564|<code>profile_source_event_id</code>. <code>TB-BUNDLE-PROFILE-N1</code> copies\n4565|the stale Session Record value, <code>TB-BUNDLE-PROFILE-N2</code> uses null as\n4566|the source, and <code>TB-BUNDLE-PROFILE-N3</code> names a losing or non-newest\n4567|event. Each is <code>task_board_bundle_invalid</code> before import.\n4568|\n4569|<code>tb-session-bundle-v1</code> is a deterministic POSIX PAX tar archive with\n4570|exactly these regular-file members for the primary example, in this bytewise\n4571|path order:\n4572|\n4573|~~~text\n4574|blobs/sha256/cc/cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\n4575|blobs/sha256/dd/dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd\n4576|blobs/sha256/ee/eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\n4577|bundle.json\n4578|~~~\n4579|\n4580|For a digest <code>sha256:H</code>, where <code>H</code> is exactly 64\n4581|lowercase hexadecimal characters, the one archive member is\n4582|<code>blobs/sha256/H[0:2]/H[2:64]</code>. The shard is the first two hex\n4583|characters and the leaf is the remaining 62; neither component contains the\n4584|<code>sha256:</code> prefix or the full digest. This is Section 3.2\n4585|<code>digest_path_v1</code> beneath the archive's <code>blobs/</code> prefix;\n4586|there is no second storage grammar. The required blob set is the\n4587|set-union of <code>provider_snapshot.blob_id</code>,\n4588|<code>manager_record.blob_id</code>, and non-null\n4589|<code>native_goal_binding.opaque_blob_id</code>. Two fields naming the same\n4590|digest produce one member.\n4591|\n4592|The archive MUST contain exactly <code>bundle.json</code> plus one regular file\n4593|for each member of that set. Directory entries, PAX global or per-file extended\n4594|headers, GNU long-name records, links, devices, sparse files, and any other\n4595|member are forbidden. All v1 member names fit the base POSIX header fields;\n4596|exporters MUST fail with <code>task_board_bundle_invalid</code> rather than emit\n4597|an extension header. Members are sorted\n4598|bytewise by complete path and use uid/gid 0, empty owner/group names, timestamp\n4599|0, and mode 0600. <code>bundle.json</code> is the UTF-8 JCS encoding of the\n4600|complete displayed object including <code>bundle_id</code>, with no BOM or\n4601|trailing newline. Each blob member contains its raw bytes and MUST hash to the\n4602|digest from which its path was derived.\n4603|\n4604|Compression is not part of the bundle contract; the outer Transfer Manifest\n4605|MAY content-address a compressed transport blob. <code>bundle_id</code> is the\n4606|canonical digest of the logical <code>bundle.json</code> object with only\n4607|<code>bundle_id</code> omitted. Because that object names every required opaque\n4608|blob by digest, it transitively identifies all bundle content.\n4609|<code>TB-ARCHIVE-PATH-POS</code> is the exact four-member set above.\n4610|<code>TB-ARCHIVE-PATH-N1</code> uses the full digest as the leaf,\n4611|<code>TB-ARCHIVE-PATH-N2</code> uses a wrong shard,\n4612|<code>TB-ARCHIVE-PATH-N3</code> adds a directory/unreferenced member, and\n4613|<code>TB-ARCHIVE-PATH-N4</code> changes one raw blob byte. Each MUST fail before\n4614|import/open. The importer also rejects a missing member, duplicate path, unsafe\n4615|path, noncanonical <code>bundle.json</code>, or digest mismatch.\n4616|\n4617|### 9.4 Local and remote boards\n4618|\n4619|For a local file-backed board, the workspace manifest MUST include the entire\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
