{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":720,"recorded_at":1780531400001435,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcc-8f28-79d1-a2ff-46b83dc83a8a"},"task_id":"01a0adcc-8f28-79d1-a2ff-46b83dc83a8a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adcc-8f28-79d1-a2ff-46b83dc83a8a","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/identity.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\t\"regexp\"\n6|\t\"strings\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// This file validates the Provider Identity Record (Section 5.5,\n12|// urn:ax:schema:provider-identity 1.0.0) the host reads from\n13|// identify-session results and carries in launch, resume, quiesce,\n14|// and fork bodies, plus the identify-session success wrapper. The\n15|// record_id is required to be a digest but is not recomputed here:\n16|// content addressing belongs to the object-identity story, and this\n17|// package holds no canonical encoder. The opaque_identity absolute\n18|// prefix rule mirrors the decidable half of the Section 5.5\n19|// sentence: a value beginning with an absolute path is refused, and\n20|// an embedded path the prefix cannot see is a stated bound.\n21|//\n22|// CheckIdentity validates the record shape in this package's provider-stdio\n23|// dialect (provider_protocol_error with member attribution, which the\n24|// shared package cannot mint) and conjoins the verdict with the owner's\n25|// production identity entry canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity: the two\n26|// validators must agree on the Section 5.5 shape rule for rule, and a\n27|// document the dialect admits but the owner refuses is refused at the\n28|// owner gate below. The decoder half of that agreement is pinned by the\n29|// derived TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON sweep,\n30|// which judges escape and raw-UTF-8 vectors through the shared\n31|// decodeStrictObject every entry here reads through, and any shape-rule\n32|// change must land in both validators in the same change.\n33|//\n34|// Binding verification split, stated plainly: the three terminal\n35|// schemas verify their identity binding — terminalbackend's Parse\n36|// entries recompute the omit-self digest and refuse a mismatched claim\n37|// — while provider-identity records admitted here do not. CheckIdentity\n38|// requires record_id to be a well-formed digest but never recomputes\n39|// it, and the conjoined CalculateObjectIdentity entry validates shape\n40|// only (its digest return is discarded below); the entry that would\n41|// attest the binding, canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity, has no\n42|// production call site attesting provider-identity records. The only\n43|// production call sites (internal/sessrepo, TASK-260830-wbpf1v) attest\n44|// session-record and session-event bindings — and the load\n45|// re-verification among them does recompute whatever digest stored\n46|// bytes claim, including a provider-identity one, before refusing it.\n47|// The two entry decodes refuse any other schema before Verify; the\n48|// load path re-verifies stored blobs through Verify and refuses a\n49|// non-event_id self field or an index-disagreeing digest at its named\n50|// arms (pinned in that leaf by\n51|// TestLoadRefusesProviderIdentityBlobAtEventPath and\n52|// TestLoadRefusesSwappedEventBlobs). So no transport gate and no\n53|// persistence path attests a provider-identity binding today; the one\n54|// path that recomputes such a digest refuses it. An earlier revision\n55|// of this comment claimed a schema gate in front of every Verify call,\n56|// which the load site never had; that false universal is withdrawn\n57|// here.\n58|//\n59|// This is deferred, not decided. Conjoining Verify here would refuse\n60|// records this gate documents as admitted: every boundary admission in\n61|// identity_test.go mutates content while keeping the example record_id,\n62|// so its claim no longer matches recomputation. Changing that admission\n63|// contract needs the identity owner's ruling on what a mismatched live\n64|// binding must do (refuse? re-resolve? at which layer?), which this leaf\n65|// cannot give for another owner's entry point. Until that ruling lands\n66|// — wired as a board element after this story's final leaf closes —\n67|// this gate admits any well-formed digest, and says so.\n68|//\n69|// The earlier justification for the deferral is withdrawn as false: it\n70|// claimed the gate must admit the pinned Section 5.5 example whose\n71|// record_id is merely illustrative. Measured in\n72|// TestSpecIdentityExampleVerifiesAgainstItsClaimedDigest, Verify returns\n73|// the example's own record_id with nil error, so the example IS the true\n74|// omit-self digest and cannot justify skipping attestation.\n75|\n76|// identitySchema is the exact schema identifier the record carries.\n77|const identitySchema = \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\"\n78|\n79|// identitySchemaVersion is the only identity version accepted.\n80|const identitySchemaVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n81|\n82|// identityKinds is the closed identity-kind enum in section order.\n83|var identityKinds = []string{\n84|\t\"session_uuid\",\n85|\t\"session_path_or_id\",\n86|\t\"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n87|\t\"task_board_managed\",\n88|\t\"provider_defined\",\n89|}\n90|\n91|// identityMembers is the exact required member set of a Provider\n92|// Identity Record.\n93|var identityMembers = map[string]bool{\n94|\t\"schema\":                    true,\n95|\t\"schema_version\":            true,\n96|\t\"record_id\":                 true,\n97|\t\"subject_id\":                true,\n98|\t\"session_id\":                true,\n99|\t\"provider_id\":               true,\n100|\t\"provider_version\":          true,\n101|\t\"provider_version_range\":    true,\n102|\t\"native_session_id\":         true,\n103|\t\"identity_kind\":             true,\n104|\t\"logical_workspace_id\":      true,\n105|\t\"backend_realm_fingerprint\": true,\n106|\t\"opaque_identity\":           true,\n107|\t\"created_by_host_id\":        true,\n108|\t\"created_at\":                true,\n109|\t\"extensions\":                true,\n110|}\n111|\n112|// identityRequired lists identityMembers in a fixed order so a record\n113|// missing several members always names the same one.\n114|var identityRequired = []string{\n115|\t\"schema\",\n116|\t\"schema_version\",\n117|\t\"record_id\",\n118|\t\"subject_id\",\n119|\t\"session_id\",\n120|\t\"provider_id\",\n121|\t\"provider_version\",\n122|\t\"provider_version_range\",\n123|\t\"native_session_id\",\n124|\t\"identity_kind\",\n125|\t\"logical_workspace_id\",\n126|\t\"backend_realm_fingerprint\",\n127|\t\"opaque_identity\",\n128|\t\"created_by_host_id\",\n129|\t\"created_at\",\n130|\t\"extensions\",\n131|}\n132|\n133|// identityKeyPattern is the provider-identity key grammar Section 5.5\n134|// states: [a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}.\n135|var identityKeyPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}$`)\n136|\n137|// windowsDrivePattern matches a Windows drive-qualified absolute\n138|// prefix: a letter, a colon, and a separator.\n139|var windowsDrivePattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z]:[\\\\/]`)\n140|\n141|// CheckIdentity validates one Provider Identity Record naming the\n142|// expected provider. Shape violations are provider_protocol_errors;\n143|// a well-formed record for another provider is an invalid_config\n144|// caller error: the caller correlated the wrong identity to this\n145|// session.\n146|func CheckIdentity(body []byte, wantProviderID string) error {\n147|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n148|\tif fault != nil {\n149|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n150|\t\tif err != nil {\n151|\t\t\treturn err\n152|\t\t}\n153|\t\treturn failure\n154|\t}\n155|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, identityMembers); unknown {\n156|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity carries unknown member\", name)\n157|\t\tif err != nil {\n158|\t\t\treturn err\n159|\t\t}\n160|\t\treturn failure\n161|\t}\n162|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, identityRequired); missing {\n163|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity misses a required member\", name)\n164|\t\tif err != nil {\n165|\t\t\treturn err\n166|\t\t}\n167|\t\treturn failure\n168|\t}\n169|\tif schema, ok := rawString(members[\"schema\"]); !ok || schema != identitySchema {\n170|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity schema is not the provider identity\", \"schema\")\n171|\t\tif err != nil {\n172|\t\t\treturn err\n173|\t\t}\n174|\t\treturn failure\n175|\t}\n176|\tif version, ok := rawString(members[\"schema_version\"]); !ok || version != identitySchemaVersion {\n177|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity schema_version is not 1.0.0\", \"schema_version\")\n178|\t\tif err != nil {\n179|\t\t\treturn err\n180|\t\t}\n181|\t\treturn failure\n182|\t}\n183|\tif digest, ok := rawString(members[\"record_id\"]); !ok || !isDigest(digest) {\n184|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity record_id is not a digest\", \"record_id\")\n185|\t\tif err != nil {\n186|\t\t\treturn err\n187|\t\t}\n188|\t\treturn failure\n189|\t}\n190|\tsubject, ok := rawString(members[\"subject_id\"])\n191|\tif !ok || !isUUIDv7(subject) {\n192|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity subject_id is not a UUIDv7\", \"subject_id\")\n193|\t\tif err != nil {\n194|\t\t\treturn err\n195|\t\t}\n196|\t\treturn failure\n197|\t}\n198|\tsession, ok := rawString(members[\"session_id\"])\n199|\tif !ok || !isUUIDv7(session) {\n200|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity session_id is not a UUIDv7\", \"session_id\")\n201|\t\tif err != nil {\n202|\t\t\treturn err\n203|\t\t}\n204|\t\treturn failure\n205|\t}\n206|\tif subject != session {\n207|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity subject_id does not equal session_id\", \"subject_id\")\n208|\t\tif err != nil {\n209|\t\t\treturn err\n210|\t\t}\n211|\t\treturn failure\n212|\t}\n213|\tprovider, ok := rawString(members[\"provider_id\"])\n214|\tif !ok || !validProviderID(provider) {\n215|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_id is not a provider id\", \"provider_id\")\n216|\t\tif err != nil {\n217|\t\t\treturn err\n218|\t\t}\n219|\t\treturn failure\n220|\t}\n221|\tif provider != wantProviderID {\n222|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"identity names another provider\")\n223|\t\tif err != nil {\n224|\t\t\treturn err\n225|\t\t}\n226|\t\treturn failure\n227|\t}\n228|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"provider_version\"], 1, 128) {\n229|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_version is not 1..128 characters\", \"provider_version\")\n230|\t\tif err != nil {\n231|\t\t\treturn err\n232|\t\t}\n233|\t\treturn failure\n234|\t}\n235|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"provider_version_range\"], 1, 256) {\n236|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_version_range is not 1..256 characters\", \"provider_version_range\")\n237|\t\tif err != nil {\n238|\t\t\treturn err\n239|\t\t}\n240|\t\treturn failure\n241|\t}\n242|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"native_session_id\"], 1, 512) {\n243|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity native_session_id is not 1..512 characters\", \"native_session_id\")\n244|\t\tif err != nil {\n245|\t\t\treturn err\n246|\t\t}\n247|\t\treturn failure\n248|\t}\n249|\tkind, ok := rawString(members[\"identity_kind\"])\n250|\tif !ok || !isIdentityKind(kind) {\n251|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity kind is not a registry member\", \"identity_kind\")\n252|\t\tif err != nil {\n253|\t\t\treturn err\n254|\t\t}\n255|\t\treturn failure\n256|\t}\n257|\tif workspace, ok := rawString(members[\"logical_workspace_id\"]); !ok || !isUUIDv7(workspace) {\n258|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity workspace is not a UUIDv7\", \"logical_workspace_id\")\n259|\t\tif err != nil {\n260|\t\t\treturn err\n261|\t\t}\n262|\t\treturn failure\n263|\t}\n264|\tif err := checkIdentityRealm(members[\"backend_realm_fingerprint\"], provider, kind); err != nil {\n265|\t\treturn err\n266|\t}\n267|\tif err := checkIdentityOpaque(members[\"opaque_identity\"]); err != nil {\n268|\t\treturn err\n269|\t}\n270|\tif host, ok := rawString(members[\"created_by_host_id\"]); !ok || !isUUIDv7(host) {\n271|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity host is not a UUIDv7\", \"created_by_host_id\")\n272|\t\tif err != nil {\n273|\t\t\treturn err\n274|\t\t}\n275|\t\treturn failure\n276|\t}\n277|\tif created, ok := rawString(members[\"created_at\"]); !ok || !isTimestamp(created) {\n278|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity timestamp is not a timestamp\", \"created_at\")\n279|\t\tif err != nil {\n280|\t\t\treturn err\n281|\t\t}\n282|\t\treturn failure\n283|\t}\n284|\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"extensions\"]) {\n285|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity extensions is not an object\", \"extensions\")\n286|\t\tif err != nil {\n287|\t\t\treturn err\n288|\t\t}\n289|\t\treturn failure\n290|\t}\n291|\t// The member arms above are this package's provider-stdio dialect of\n292|\t// the Section 5.5 rule; the owner of that rule is canonicaljson\n293|\t// (validateProviderIdentityRecord, registered for section:5.5 in the\n294|\t// traceability registry), and the dialect keeps its member attribution\n295|\t// deliberately. The verdict is therefore conjoined with the owner's\n296|\t// production identity entry: a document this dialect admits but the\n297|\t// owner refuses — open extensions content, a number the dialect never\n298|\t// reads, nesting beyond the dialect's view — is refused here rather\n299|\t// than admitted through a drifted copy. The provider-equality\n300|\t// correlation above stays host-side: it is a caller rule, not a\n301|\t// content rule, and the owner never sees it.\n302|\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(body); err != nil {\n303|\t\tfailure, ferr := failProtocol(\"identity is not a valid provider identity\", \"\")\n304|\t\tif ferr != nil {\n305|\t\t\treturn ferr\n306|\t\t}\n307|\t\treturn failure\n308|\t}\n309|\treturn nil\n310|}\n311|\n312|// checkIdentityRealm enforces the digest-or-null shape and the one\n313|// conditional rule Section 5.5 states: an Antigravity\n314|// backend_conversation_uuid MUST carry a non-null realm fingerprint,\n315|// because the backend realm is a resume precondition there.\n316|func checkIdentityRealm(raw json.RawMessage, provider, kind string) error {\n317|\trealm, isNull, ok := rawNullableString(raw)\n318|\tif !ok || (!isNull && !isDigest(realm)) {\n319|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity realm is not a digest or null\", \"backend_realm_fingerprint\")\n320|\t\tif err != nil {\n321|\t\t\treturn err\n322|\t\t}\n323|\t\treturn failure\n324|\t}\n325|\tif provider == \"antigravity\" && kind == \"backend_conversation_uuid\" && isNull {\n326|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity realm is required for this backend kind\", \"backend_realm_fingerprint\")\n327|\t\tif err != nil {\n328|\t\t\treturn err\n329|\t\t}\n330|\t\treturn failure\n331|\t}\n332|\treturn nil\n333|}\n334|\n335|// checkIdentityOpaque enforces the explicit adapter-data surface: an\n336|// object of at most 32 entries, keyed by the provider-identity key\n337|// grammar, with non-secret string values of 1..1,024 characters that\n338|// MUST NOT begin with an absolute path.\n339|func checkIdentityOpaque(raw json.RawMessage) error {\n340|\topaque, fault := decodeStrictObject(raw)\n341|\tif fault != nil {\n342|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n343|\t\tif err != nil {\n344|\t\t\treturn err\n345|\t\t}\n346|\t\treturn failure\n347|\t}\n348|\tif len(opaque) > 32 {\n349|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque_identity exceeds 32 entries\", \"opaque_identity\")\n350|\t\tif err != nil {\n351|\t\t\treturn err\n352|\t\t}\n353|\t\treturn failure\n354|\t}\n355|\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(opaque))\n356|\tfor key := range opaque {\n357|\t\tkeys = append(keys, key)\n358|\t}\n359|\tfor _, key := range keys {\n360|\t\tif !identityKeyPattern.MatchString(key) {\n361|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque key is not a provider key\", \"opaque_identity\")\n362|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n363|\t\t\t\treturn err\n364|\t\t\t}\n365|\t\t\treturn failure\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\tvalue, ok := rawString(opaque[key])\n368|\t\tif !ok || runeLength(value) < 1 || runeLength(value) > 1024 {\n369|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque value is not 1..1024 characters\", \"opaque_identity\")\n370|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n371|\t\t\t\treturn err\n372|\t\t\t}\n373|\t\t\treturn failure\n374|\t\t}\n375|\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(value, \"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(value, `\\\\`) || windowsDrivePattern.MatchString(value) {\n376|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque value begins with an absolute path\", \"opaque_identity\")\n377|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n378|\t\t\t\treturn err\n379|\t\t\t}\n380|\t\t\treturn failure\n381|\t\t}\n382|\t}\n383|\treturn nil\n384|}\n385|\n386|func isIdentityKind(value string) bool {\n387|\tfor _, kind := range identityKinds {\n388|\t\tif value == kind {\n389|\t\t\treturn true\n390|\t\t}\n391|\t}\n392|\treturn false\n393|}\n394|\n395|// identifyMembers is the exact required member set of an\n396|// identify-session success body.\n397|var identifyMembers = map[string]bool{\n398|\t\"identity\":         true,\n399|\t\"confidence\":       true,\n400|\t\"matched_evidence\": true,\n401|}\n402|\n403|// identifyRequired lists identifyMembers in a fixed order.\n404|var identifyRequired = []string{\"identity\", \"confidence\", \"matched_evidence\"}\n405|\n406|// identifyConfidences is the closed confidence vocabulary.\n407|var identifyConfidences = []string{\"exact\", \"strong\", \"weak\"}\n408|\n409|// identifyEvidence is the closed matched-evidence vocabulary.\n410|var identifyEvidence = []string{\"native_id\", \"store_path\", \"provider_event\", \"backend_lookup\"}\n411|\n412|// DecodeIdentifyResult validates one identify-session success body:\n413|// the Provider Identity Record for the expected provider, a closed\n414|// confidence, and 1..4 sorted unique matched-evidence members.\n415|func DecodeIdentifyResult(body []byte, wantProviderID string) error {\n416|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n417|\tif fault != nil {\n418|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n419|\t\tif err != nil {\n420|\t\t\treturn err\n421|\t\t}\n422|\t\treturn failure\n423|\t}\n424|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, identifyMembers); unknown {\n425|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify result carries unknown member\", name)\n426|\t\tif err != nil {\n427|\t\t\treturn err\n428|\t\t}\n429|\t\treturn failure\n430|\t}\n431|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, identifyRequired); missing {\n432|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify result misses a required member\", name)\n433|\t\tif err != nil {\n434|\t\t\treturn err\n435|\t\t}\n436|\t\treturn failure\n437|\t}\n438|\tconfidence, ok := rawString(members[\"confidence\"])\n439|\tif !ok || !isIdentifyConfidence(confidence) {\n440|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify confidence is not exact strong or weak\", \"confidence\")\n441|\t\tif err != nil {\n442|\t\t\treturn err\n443|\t\t}\n444|\t\treturn failure\n445|\t}\n446|\tif err := checkIdentifyEvidence(members[\"matched_evidence\"]); err != nil {\n447|\t\treturn err\n448|\t}\n449|\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"identity\"]) {\n450|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify identity is not an object\", \"identity\")\n451|\t\tif err != nil {\n452|\t\t\treturn err\n453|\t\t}\n454|\t\treturn failure\n455|\t}\n456|\tif err := CheckIdentity(members[\"identity\"], wantProviderID); err != nil {\n457|\t\treturn err\n458|\t}\n459|\treturn nil\n460|}\n461|\n462|func isIdentifyConfidence(value string) bool {\n463|\tfor _, confidence := range identifyConfidences {\n464|\t\tif value == confidence {\n465|\t\t\treturn true\n466|\t\t}\n467|\t}\n468|\treturn false\n469|}\n470|\n471|// checkIdentifyEvidence requires 1..4 sorted unique closed-vocabulary\n472|// evidence members: the observation must cite what matched, exactly\n473|// once each.\n474|func checkIdentifyEvidence(raw json.RawMessage) error {\n475|\tevidence, ok := rawStringArray(raw)\n476|\tif !ok || len(evidence) < 1 || len(evidence) > 4 {\n477|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence is not 1..4 members\", \"matched_evidence\")\n478|\t\tif err != nil {\n479|\t\t\treturn err\n480|\t\t}\n481|\t\treturn failure\n482|\t}\n483|\tallowed := map[string]bool{}\n484|\tfor _, member := range identifyEvidence {\n485|\t\tallowed[member] = true\n486|\t}\n487|\tfor _, member := range evidence {\n488|\t\tif !allowed[member] {\n489|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence names an unknown member\", \"matched_evidence\")\n490|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n491|\t\t\t\treturn err\n492|\t\t\t}\n493|\t\t\treturn failure\n494|\t\t}\n495|\t}\n496|\tif !sortedUniqueStrings(evidence) {\n497|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence is not sorted unique\", \"matched_evidence\")\n498|\t\tif err != nil {\n499|\t\t\treturn err\n500|\t\t}\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8ed","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":721,"recorded_at":1780531400001437,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adcc-8f28-79d1-a2ff-46b83dc83a8a"},"task_id":"01a0adcc-8f28-79d1-a2ff-46b83dc83a8a","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0adcc-8f28-79d1-a2ff-46b83dc83a8a"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8ef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":722,"recorded_at":1780531400001439,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0adcc8cb873ec936114e36eca6da9","text":"Read text file `internal/provhost/identity.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\t\"regexp\"\n6|\t\"strings\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// This file validates the Provider Identity Record (Section 5.5,\n12|// urn:ax:schema:provider-identity 1.0.0) the host reads from\n13|// identify-session results and carries in launch, resume, quiesce,\n14|// and fork bodies, plus the identify-session success wrapper. The\n15|// record_id is required to be a digest but is not recomputed here:\n16|// content addressing belongs to the object-identity story, and this\n17|// package holds no canonical encoder. The opaque_identity absolute\n18|// prefix rule mirrors the decidable half of the Section 5.5\n19|// sentence: a value beginning with an absolute path is refused, and\n20|// an embedded path the prefix cannot see is a stated bound.\n21|//\n22|// CheckIdentity validates the record shape in this package's provider-stdio\n23|// dialect (provider_protocol_error with member attribution, which the\n24|// shared package cannot mint) and conjoins the verdict with the owner's\n25|// production identity entry canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity: the two\n26|// validators must agree on the Section 5.5 shape rule for rule, and a\n27|// document the dialect admits but the owner refuses is refused at the\n28|// owner gate below. The decoder half of that agreement is pinned by the\n29|// derived TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON sweep,\n30|// which judges escape and raw-UTF-8 vectors through the shared\n31|// decodeStrictObject every entry here reads through, and any shape-rule\n32|// change must land in both validators in the same change.\n33|//\n34|// Binding verification split, stated plainly: the three terminal\n35|// schemas verify their identity binding — terminalbackend's Parse\n36|// entries recompute the omit-self digest and refuse a mismatched claim\n37|// — while provider-identity records admitted here do not. CheckIdentity\n38|// requires record_id to be a well-formed digest but never recomputes\n39|// it, and the conjoined CalculateObjectIdentity entry validates shape\n40|// only (its digest return is discarded below); the entry that would\n41|// attest the binding, canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity, has no\n42|// production call site attesting provider-identity records. The only\n43|// production call sites (internal/sessrepo, TASK-260830-wbpf1v) attest\n44|// session-record and session-event bindings — and the load\n45|// re-verification among them does recompute whatever digest stored\n46|// bytes claim, including a provider-identity one, before refusing it.\n47|// The two entry decodes refuse any other schema before Verify; the\n48|// load path re-verifies stored blobs through Verify and refuses a\n49|// non-event_id self field or an index-disagreeing digest at its named\n50|// arms (pinned in that leaf by\n51|// TestLoadRefusesProviderIdentityBlobAtEventPath and\n52|// TestLoadRefusesSwappedEventBlobs). So no transport gate and no\n53|// persistence path attests a provider-identity binding today; the one\n54|// path that recomputes such a digest refuses it. An earlier revision\n55|// of this comment claimed a schema gate in front of every Verify call,\n56|// which the load site never had; that false universal is withdrawn\n57|// here.\n58|//\n59|// This is deferred, not decided. Conjoining Verify here would refuse\n60|// records this gate documents as admitted: every boundary admission in\n61|// identity_test.go mutates content while keeping the example record_id,\n62|// so its claim no longer matches recomputation. Changing that admission\n63|// contract needs the identity owner's ruling on what a mismatched live\n64|// binding must do (refuse? re-resolve? at which layer?), which this leaf\n65|// cannot give for another owner's entry point. Until that ruling lands\n66|// — wired as a board element after this story's final leaf closes —\n67|// this gate admits any well-formed digest, and says so.\n68|//\n69|// The earlier justification for the deferral is withdrawn as false: it\n70|// claimed the gate must admit the pinned Section 5.5 example whose\n71|// record_id is merely illustrative. Measured in\n72|// TestSpecIdentityExampleVerifiesAgainstItsClaimedDigest, Verify returns\n73|// the example's own record_id with nil error, so the example IS the true\n74|// omit-self digest and cannot justify skipping attestation.\n75|\n76|// identitySchema is the exact schema identifier the record carries.\n77|const identitySchema = \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\"\n78|\n79|// identitySchemaVersion is the only identity version accepted.\n80|const identitySchemaVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n81|\n82|// identityKinds is the closed identity-kind enum in section order.\n83|var identityKinds = []string{\n84|\t\"session_uuid\",\n85|\t\"session_path_or_id\",\n86|\t\"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n87|\t\"task_board_managed\",\n88|\t\"provider_defined\",\n89|}\n90|\n91|// identityMembers is the exact required member set of a Provider\n92|// Identity Record.\n93|var identityMembers = map[string]bool{\n94|\t\"schema\":                    true,\n95|\t\"schema_version\":            true,\n96|\t\"record_id\":                 true,\n97|\t\"subject_id\":                true,\n98|\t\"session_id\":                true,\n99|\t\"provider_id\":               true,\n100|\t\"provider_version\":          true,\n101|\t\"provider_version_range\":    true,\n102|\t\"native_session_id\":         true,\n103|\t\"identity_kind\":             true,\n104|\t\"logical_workspace_id\":      true,\n105|\t\"backend_realm_fingerprint\": true,\n106|\t\"opaque_identity\":           true,\n107|\t\"created_by_host_id\":        true,\n108|\t\"created_at\":                true,\n109|\t\"extensions\":                true,\n110|}\n111|\n112|// identityRequired lists identityMembers in a fixed order so a record\n113|// missing several members always names the same one.\n114|var identityRequired = []string{\n115|\t\"schema\",\n116|\t\"schema_version\",\n117|\t\"record_id\",\n118|\t\"subject_id\",\n119|\t\"session_id\",\n120|\t\"provider_id\",\n121|\t\"provider_version\",\n122|\t\"provider_version_range\",\n123|\t\"native_session_id\",\n124|\t\"identity_kind\",\n125|\t\"logical_workspace_id\",\n126|\t\"backend_realm_fingerprint\",\n127|\t\"opaque_identity\",\n128|\t\"created_by_host_id\",\n129|\t\"created_at\",\n130|\t\"extensions\",\n131|}\n132|\n133|// identityKeyPattern is the provider-identity key grammar Section 5.5\n134|// states: [a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}.\n135|var identityKeyPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}$`)\n136|\n137|// windowsDrivePattern matches a Windows drive-qualified absolute\n138|// prefix: a letter, a colon, and a separator.\n139|var windowsDrivePattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z]:[\\\\/]`)\n140|\n141|// CheckIdentity validates one Provider Identity Record naming the\n142|// expected provider. Shape violations are provider_protocol_errors;\n143|// a well-formed record for another provider is an invalid_config\n144|// caller error: the caller correlated the wrong identity to this\n145|// session.\n146|func CheckIdentity(body []byte, wantProviderID string) error {\n147|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n148|\tif fault != nil {\n149|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n150|\t\tif err != nil {\n151|\t\t\treturn err\n152|\t\t}\n153|\t\treturn failure\n154|\t}\n155|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, identityMembers); unknown {\n156|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity carries unknown member\", name)\n157|\t\tif err != nil {\n158|\t\t\treturn err\n159|\t\t}\n160|\t\treturn failure\n161|\t}\n162|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, identityRequired); missing {\n163|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity misses a required member\", name)\n164|\t\tif err != nil {\n165|\t\t\treturn err\n166|\t\t}\n167|\t\treturn failure\n168|\t}\n169|\tif schema, ok := rawString(members[\"schema\"]); !ok || schema != identitySchema {\n170|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity schema is not the provider identity\", \"schema\")\n171|\t\tif err != nil {\n172|\t\t\treturn err\n173|\t\t}\n174|\t\treturn failure\n175|\t}\n176|\tif version, ok := rawString(members[\"schema_version\"]); !ok || version != identitySchemaVersion {\n177|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity schema_version is not 1.0.0\", \"schema_version\")\n178|\t\tif err != nil {\n179|\t\t\treturn err\n180|\t\t}\n181|\t\treturn failure\n182|\t}\n183|\tif digest, ok := rawString(members[\"record_id\"]); !ok || !isDigest(digest) {\n184|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity record_id is not a digest\", \"record_id\")\n185|\t\tif err != nil {\n186|\t\t\treturn err\n187|\t\t}\n188|\t\treturn failure\n189|\t}\n190|\tsubject, ok := rawString(members[\"subject_id\"])\n191|\tif !ok || !isUUIDv7(subject) {\n192|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity subject_id is not a UUIDv7\", \"subject_id\")\n193|\t\tif err != nil {\n194|\t\t\treturn err\n195|\t\t}\n196|\t\treturn failure\n197|\t}\n198|\tsession, ok := rawString(members[\"session_id\"])\n199|\tif !ok || !isUUIDv7(session) {\n200|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity session_id is not a UUIDv7\", \"session_id\")\n201|\t\tif err != nil {\n202|\t\t\treturn err\n203|\t\t}\n204|\t\treturn failure\n205|\t}\n206|\tif subject != session {\n207|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity subject_id does not equal session_id\", \"subject_id\")\n208|\t\tif err != nil {\n209|\t\t\treturn err\n210|\t\t}\n211|\t\treturn failure\n212|\t}\n213|\tprovider, ok := rawString(members[\"provider_id\"])\n214|\tif !ok || !validProviderID(provider) {\n215|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_id is not a provider id\", \"provider_id\")\n216|\t\tif err != nil {\n217|\t\t\treturn err\n218|\t\t}\n219|\t\treturn failure\n220|\t}\n221|\tif provider != wantProviderID {\n222|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"identity names another provider\")\n223|\t\tif err != nil {\n224|\t\t\treturn err\n225|\t\t}\n226|\t\treturn failure\n227|\t}\n228|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"provider_version\"], 1, 128) {\n229|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_version is not 1..128 characters\", \"provider_version\")\n230|\t\tif err != nil {\n231|\t\t\treturn err\n232|\t\t}\n233|\t\treturn failure\n234|\t}\n235|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"provider_version_range\"], 1, 256) {\n236|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity provider_version_range is not 1..256 characters\", \"provider_version_range\")\n237|\t\tif err != nil {\n238|\t\t\treturn err\n239|\t\t}\n240|\t\treturn failure\n241|\t}\n242|\tif !isBoundedString(members[\"native_session_id\"], 1, 512) {\n243|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity native_session_id is not 1..512 characters\", \"native_session_id\")\n244|\t\tif err != nil {\n245|\t\t\treturn err\n246|\t\t}\n247|\t\treturn failure\n248|\t}\n249|\tkind, ok := rawString(members[\"identity_kind\"])\n250|\tif !ok || !isIdentityKind(kind) {\n251|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity kind is not a registry member\", \"identity_kind\")\n252|\t\tif err != nil {\n253|\t\t\treturn err\n254|\t\t}\n255|\t\treturn failure\n256|\t}\n257|\tif workspace, ok := rawString(members[\"logical_workspace_id\"]); !ok || !isUUIDv7(workspace) {\n258|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity workspace is not a UUIDv7\", \"logical_workspace_id\")\n259|\t\tif err != nil {\n260|\t\t\treturn err\n261|\t\t}\n262|\t\treturn failure\n263|\t}\n264|\tif err := checkIdentityRealm(members[\"backend_realm_fingerprint\"], provider, kind); err != nil {\n265|\t\treturn err\n266|\t}\n267|\tif err := checkIdentityOpaque(members[\"opaque_identity\"]); err != nil {\n268|\t\treturn err\n269|\t}\n270|\tif host, ok := rawString(members[\"created_by_host_id\"]); !ok || !isUUIDv7(host) {\n271|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity host is not a UUIDv7\", \"created_by_host_id\")\n272|\t\tif err != nil {\n273|\t\t\treturn err\n274|\t\t}\n275|\t\treturn failure\n276|\t}\n277|\tif created, ok := rawString(members[\"created_at\"]); !ok || !isTimestamp(created) {\n278|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity timestamp is not a timestamp\", \"created_at\")\n279|\t\tif err != nil {\n280|\t\t\treturn err\n281|\t\t}\n282|\t\treturn failure\n283|\t}\n284|\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"extensions\"]) {\n285|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity extensions is not an object\", \"extensions\")\n286|\t\tif err != nil {\n287|\t\t\treturn err\n288|\t\t}\n289|\t\treturn failure\n290|\t}\n291|\t// The member arms above are this package's provider-stdio dialect of\n292|\t// the Section 5.5 rule; the owner of that rule is canonicaljson\n293|\t// (validateProviderIdentityRecord, registered for section:5.5 in the\n294|\t// traceability registry), and the dialect keeps its member attribution\n295|\t// deliberately. The verdict is therefore conjoined with the owner's\n296|\t// production identity entry: a document this dialect admits but the\n297|\t// owner refuses — open extensions content, a number the dialect never\n298|\t// reads, nesting beyond the dialect's view — is refused here rather\n299|\t// than admitted through a drifted copy. The provider-equality\n300|\t// correlation above stays host-side: it is a caller rule, not a\n301|\t// content rule, and the owner never sees it.\n302|\tif _, _, err := canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity(body); err != nil {\n303|\t\tfailure, ferr := failProtocol(\"identity is not a valid provider identity\", \"\")\n304|\t\tif ferr != nil {\n305|\t\t\treturn ferr\n306|\t\t}\n307|\t\treturn failure\n308|\t}\n309|\treturn nil\n310|}\n311|\n312|// checkIdentityRealm enforces the digest-or-null shape and the one\n313|// conditional rule Section 5.5 states: an Antigravity\n314|// backend_conversation_uuid MUST carry a non-null realm fingerprint,\n315|// because the backend realm is a resume precondition there.\n316|func checkIdentityRealm(raw json.RawMessage, provider, kind string) error {\n317|\trealm, isNull, ok := rawNullableString(raw)\n318|\tif !ok || (!isNull && !isDigest(realm)) {\n319|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity realm is not a digest or null\", \"backend_realm_fingerprint\")\n320|\t\tif err != nil {\n321|\t\t\treturn err\n322|\t\t}\n323|\t\treturn failure\n324|\t}\n325|\tif provider == \"antigravity\" && kind == \"backend_conversation_uuid\" && isNull {\n326|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity realm is required for this backend kind\", \"backend_realm_fingerprint\")\n327|\t\tif err != nil {\n328|\t\t\treturn err\n329|\t\t}\n330|\t\treturn failure\n331|\t}\n332|\treturn nil\n333|}\n334|\n335|// checkIdentityOpaque enforces the explicit adapter-data surface: an\n336|// object of at most 32 entries, keyed by the provider-identity key\n337|// grammar, with non-secret string values of 1..1,024 characters that\n338|// MUST NOT begin with an absolute path.\n339|func checkIdentityOpaque(raw json.RawMessage) error {\n340|\topaque, fault := decodeStrictObject(raw)\n341|\tif fault != nil {\n342|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n343|\t\tif err != nil {\n344|\t\t\treturn err\n345|\t\t}\n346|\t\treturn failure\n347|\t}\n348|\tif len(opaque) > 32 {\n349|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque_identity exceeds 32 entries\", \"opaque_identity\")\n350|\t\tif err != nil {\n351|\t\t\treturn err\n352|\t\t}\n353|\t\treturn failure\n354|\t}\n355|\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(opaque))\n356|\tfor key := range opaque {\n357|\t\tkeys = append(keys, key)\n358|\t}\n359|\tfor _, key := range keys {\n360|\t\tif !identityKeyPattern.MatchString(key) {\n361|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque key is not a provider key\", \"opaque_identity\")\n362|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n363|\t\t\t\treturn err\n364|\t\t\t}\n365|\t\t\treturn failure\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\tvalue, ok := rawString(opaque[key])\n368|\t\tif !ok || runeLength(value) < 1 || runeLength(value) > 1024 {\n369|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque value is not 1..1024 characters\", \"opaque_identity\")\n370|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n371|\t\t\t\treturn err\n372|\t\t\t}\n373|\t\t\treturn failure\n374|\t\t}\n375|\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(value, \"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(value, `\\\\`) || windowsDrivePattern.MatchString(value) {\n376|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identity opaque value begins with an absolute path\", \"opaque_identity\")\n377|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n378|\t\t\t\treturn err\n379|\t\t\t}\n380|\t\t\treturn failure\n381|\t\t}\n382|\t}\n383|\treturn nil\n384|}\n385|\n386|func isIdentityKind(value string) bool {\n387|\tfor _, kind := range identityKinds {\n388|\t\tif value == kind {\n389|\t\t\treturn true\n390|\t\t}\n391|\t}\n392|\treturn false\n393|}\n394|\n395|// identifyMembers is the exact required member set of an\n396|// identify-session success body.\n397|var identifyMembers = map[string]bool{\n398|\t\"identity\":         true,\n399|\t\"confidence\":       true,\n400|\t\"matched_evidence\": true,\n401|}\n402|\n403|// identifyRequired lists identifyMembers in a fixed order.\n404|var identifyRequired = []string{\"identity\", \"confidence\", \"matched_evidence\"}\n405|\n406|// identifyConfidences is the closed confidence vocabulary.\n407|var identifyConfidences = []string{\"exact\", \"strong\", \"weak\"}\n408|\n409|// identifyEvidence is the closed matched-evidence vocabulary.\n410|var identifyEvidence = []string{\"native_id\", \"store_path\", \"provider_event\", \"backend_lookup\"}\n411|\n412|// DecodeIdentifyResult validates one identify-session success body:\n413|// the Provider Identity Record for the expected provider, a closed\n414|// confidence, and 1..4 sorted unique matched-evidence members.\n415|func DecodeIdentifyResult(body []byte, wantProviderID string) error {\n416|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n417|\tif fault != nil {\n418|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n419|\t\tif err != nil {\n420|\t\t\treturn err\n421|\t\t}\n422|\t\treturn failure\n423|\t}\n424|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, identifyMembers); unknown {\n425|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify result carries unknown member\", name)\n426|\t\tif err != nil {\n427|\t\t\treturn err\n428|\t\t}\n429|\t\treturn failure\n430|\t}\n431|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, identifyRequired); missing {\n432|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify result misses a required member\", name)\n433|\t\tif err != nil {\n434|\t\t\treturn err\n435|\t\t}\n436|\t\treturn failure\n437|\t}\n438|\tconfidence, ok := rawString(members[\"confidence\"])\n439|\tif !ok || !isIdentifyConfidence(confidence) {\n440|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify confidence is not exact strong or weak\", \"confidence\")\n441|\t\tif err != nil {\n442|\t\t\treturn err\n443|\t\t}\n444|\t\treturn failure\n445|\t}\n446|\tif err := checkIdentifyEvidence(members[\"matched_evidence\"]); err != nil {\n447|\t\treturn err\n448|\t}\n449|\tif !isJSONObject(members[\"identity\"]) {\n450|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify identity is not an object\", \"identity\")\n451|\t\tif err != nil {\n452|\t\t\treturn err\n453|\t\t}\n454|\t\treturn failure\n455|\t}\n456|\tif err := CheckIdentity(members[\"identity\"], wantProviderID); err != nil {\n457|\t\treturn err\n458|\t}\n459|\treturn nil\n460|}\n461|\n462|func isIdentifyConfidence(value string) bool {\n463|\tfor _, confidence := range identifyConfidences {\n464|\t\tif value == confidence {\n465|\t\t\treturn true\n466|\t\t}\n467|\t}\n468|\treturn false\n469|}\n470|\n471|// checkIdentifyEvidence requires 1..4 sorted unique closed-vocabulary\n472|// evidence members: the observation must cite what matched, exactly\n473|// once each.\n474|func checkIdentifyEvidence(raw json.RawMessage) error {\n475|\tevidence, ok := rawStringArray(raw)\n476|\tif !ok || len(evidence) < 1 || len(evidence) > 4 {\n477|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence is not 1..4 members\", \"matched_evidence\")\n478|\t\tif err != nil {\n479|\t\t\treturn err\n480|\t\t}\n481|\t\treturn failure\n482|\t}\n483|\tallowed := map[string]bool{}\n484|\tfor _, member := range identifyEvidence {\n485|\t\tallowed[member] = true\n486|\t}\n487|\tfor _, member := range evidence {\n488|\t\tif !allowed[member] {\n489|\t\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence names an unknown member\", \"matched_evidence\")\n490|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n491|\t\t\t\treturn err\n492|\t\t\t}\n493|\t\t\treturn failure\n494|\t\t}\n495|\t}\n496|\tif !sortedUniqueStrings(evidence) {\n497|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"identify evidence is not sorted unique\", \"matched_evidence\")\n498|\t\tif err != nil {\n499|\t\t\treturn err\n500|\t\t}\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
