uses the independently versioned closed schema\\n<code>urn:ax:schema:cli-result</code>. Legacy commands select CLI Result 1.0.0\\nand Structured Error 1.0.0; every <code>session.clone.*</code> command selects\\nCLI Result 2.0.0 on success and Structured Error 1.1.0 on failure. No command\\nmay emit another registered version or retry a different major after parsing\\nbegins. Both CLI Result versions contain\\nexactly <code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\\n<code>command</code>, <code>ok = true</code>, <code>operation_id</code>\\n(UUIDv7 or null), <code>session_id</code> (UUIDv7 or null), the tagged\\n<code>body</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Failure output is one Structured\\nError object from Section 15.1, not a CLI Result with <code>ok = false</code>.\\nThe process exit status MUST equal that error's <code>exit_code</code>.\\n\\nThe following embedded CLI types are closed:\\n\\n| Type | Exact members and constraints |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| <code>CapabilitySummary</code> | <code>status:available&#124;conditional&#124;unsupported&#124;unknown</code>, <code>enabled:boolean</code>, <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code> |\\n| <code>SessionSummary</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>name:string[1..64]</code>, <code>kind:direct&#124;task_board</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>owner_host_name:string[1..64]</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>local_role:owner&#124;replica</code>, <code>state:SessionState</code>, <code>newest_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>newest_checkpoint_created_at:timestamp&#124;null</code>, <code>workspace_status:absent&#124;current&#124;staged&#124;conflict&#124;unsupported</code>, <code>capabilities:map(capability-name,CapabilitySummary)[0..7]</code>, <code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..1024]</code> |\\n| <code>PathDiff</code> | <code>path:path</code>, <code>classification:added&#124;removed&#124;modified&#124;type_changed&#124;mode_changed&#124;conflict</code>, <code>source_digest:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>destination_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\\n| <code>PeerSummary</code> | <code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>name:string[1..64]</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>reachable:boolean</code>, <code>last_successful_sync_at:timestamp&#124;null</code>, <code>degraded_codes:sorted unique string[0..1024]</code> |\\n| <code>CLIFinding</code> | <code>severity:info&#124;warning&#124;error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>, <code>remediation:string[1..4096]&#124;null</code>, <code>source:core&#124;terminal&#124;provider&#124;mesh&#124;workspace&#124;task_board</code> |\\n| <code>MaterializationSummary</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>mode:default&#124;copy&#124;worktree&#124;replace_managed_replica</code>, <code>destination_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>destination_classification:DestinationClass</code>, <code>preserved_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>committed:boolean</code>, <code>ownership_changed:boolean</code> |\\n\\nThe <code>command</code> tag selects exactly one body. Digest arrays and object\\narrays keyed by an ID are sorted bytewise by that ID:\\n\\n| Command tag | Exact body |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| <code>cancel</code> | <code>{name:string[1..64],cancelled:boolean}</code> with true required |\\n| <code>start</code> | <code>{session:SessionSummary,execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo,terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty}</code> |\\n| <code>list</code> | <code>{sessions:SessionSummary[0..65536],partial:boolean,unreachable_peer_ids:sorted unique UUIDv7[0..1024]}</code> |\\n| <code>status</code> | <code>{session:SessionSummary,process_present:boolean,active_operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,last_successful_sync:map(UUIDv7,timestamp)[0..1024]}</code> |\\n| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session:SessionSummary,mode:local&#124;remote,attached_owner_host_id:UUIDv7,detached:boolean,provider_exit_code:int32&#124;null}</code> |\\n| <code>takeover</code> | <code>{mode:graceful&#124;force,workspace_mode:whole_group&#124;separate_worktrees,destination_host_id:UUIDv7,source_host_id:UUIDv7,affected_session_ids:sorted unique UUIDv7[1..1024],lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0,lease_id:UUIDv4,checkpoint_id:digest,state:running&#124;idle&#124;stopped&#124;failed,materialized:boolean,adopted:boolean,resumed:boolean,warnings:sorted unique string[0..1024]}</code> |\\n| <code>fork</code> | <code>{source_session_id:UUIDv7,source_checkpoint_id:digest,session:SessionSummary,workspace_group_id:UUIDv7,provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone}</code> |\\n| <code>stop</code> | <code>{session:SessionSummary,graceful:boolean,checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,resumable:boolean,bootstrap_aborted:boolean,process_closed:boolean,store_closed:boolean}</code> |\\n| <code>resume</code> | <code>{session:SessionSummary,checkpoint_id:digest,terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty,native_session_id:string[1..512]}</code> |\\n| <code>sync</code> | <code>{peer_ids:sorted unique UUIDv7[1..1024],record_count:uint53,blob_count:uint53,byte_count:uint53,checkpoint_ids:sorted unique digest[0..4096],materialized:boolean,partial:boolean,transfer_id:UUIDv7&#124;null}</code> |\\n| <code>diff</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,peer_host_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,classification:identical&#124;different&#124;conflict,entries:PathDiff[0..65536]}</code> |\\n| <code>materialize</code> | <code>MaterializationSummary</code> |\\n| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{healthy:boolean,findings:CLIFinding[0..4096]}</code> |\\n| <code>logs</code> | <code>{emitting_host_id:UUIDv7,events:Observation Event[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..512]&#124;null}</code> |\\n| <code>peer.list</code> | <code>{peers:PeerSummary[0..1024]}</code> |\\n| <code>peer.probe</code> | <code>{peer:PeerSummary,contracts:map(contract-name,sorted unique semver[1..16]),round_trip_ms:uint53}</code> |\\n| <code>session.set_profile</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,previous_profile:standard&#124;yolo,new_profile:standard&#124;yolo,event_id:digest}</code> |\\n| <code>pane</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,result:attached&#124;parked&#124;resumed&#124;stopped,winning_owner_host_id:UUIDv7,lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0}</code> |\\n\\nThe umbrella <code>ax NAME</code> reports the selected action's command tag; it\\ndoes not invent a separate resolve shape. A canceled chooser uses\\n<code>cancel</code>. <code>operation_id</code> is non-null for start, takeover,\\nfork, stop, resume, sync, materialize, and profile mutation, and null for pure reads. A\\nsession-scoped command requires non-null <code>session_id</code> equal to every\\nnested Session Summary; <code>list</code>, <code>doctor</code>, and peer commands\\nuse null. The internal streaming command <code>ax rpc serve --stdio</code> is an\\nRPC protocol endpoint, not a CLI Result producer, and MUST reject\\n<code>--json</code>.\\n\\nThe CLI stop tuple is mapped losslessly from RPC <code>session.stop</code>.\\n<code>checkpoint_id = null</code> is valid only with\\n<code>graceful=false</code>, <code>resumable=false</code>,\\n<code>bootstrap_aborted=true</code>, and nested session state\\n<code>failed</code>. A non-null checkpoint with nested state\\n<code>stopped</code> requires <code>resumable=true</code> and\\n<code>bootstrap_aborted=false</code>. Process and store closure must be true in\\nevery success object; otherwise the command returns Structured Error instead.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8355,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2089,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
