{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd3f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":1274,"recorded_at":1780531400002543,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0add1-0a9f-7cc2-b76b-bd4dc86c1ac7"},"task_id":"01a0add1-0a9f-7cc2-b76b-bd4dc86c1ac7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0add1-0a9f-7cc2-b76b-bd4dc86c1ac7","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/.agents/skills/project-management/references/negative-evidence.md`.\n1|# Negative Evidence Contract\n2|\n3|A passing suite means nothing unless something in it would have failed. This\n4|file is the single source of truth for the rules that make a green check mean\n5|something, and for the incident record behind each one. The operative wording\n6|that reaches every spawned child lives in the spawn template section\n7|`Evidence That Counts`; the reviewer's licence lives in `.roles/reviewer/role.md`;\n8|the repeated-variant heuristic lives in `.roles/orchestrator/role.md`. Read this\n9|file when you need the shapes, the failure vocabulary, or the incidents that\n10|produced a rule — do not restate these rules in other documents.\n11|\n12|| Rule | Operative statement | Evidence record |\n13|| --- | --- | --- |\n14|| Negative tests for gates | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n15|| Narrowing, not deleting | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n16|| Production call site | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n17|| Absence vs failure to read | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n18|| Prove, or report nothing | spawn template, `Evidence That Counts` | this file |\n19|| Reviewer licence to defeat a gate | `.roles/reviewer/role.md` | this file |\n20|| Many variants, one unowned decision | `.roles/orchestrator/role.md` | this file |\n21|\n22|## Negative Tests For Gates\n23|\n24|Any feature that GATES, REFUSES, VALIDATES, AUTHORIZES, or ATTESTS must ship\n25|with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it is supposed to\n26|reject. A positive test proving the happy path passes is not evidence that the\n27|gate works; it is evidence that the gate is reachable.\n28|\n29|This is the dominant defect class in this repository's 2026-07-28..08-03 waves.\n30|Every instance below was found because a reviewer deliberately attacked the\n31|gate, not because anyone read the code:\n32|\n33|- the fact-assay attested a COLD child that never inherited the context, because\n34|  it checked inventory, session id, digests, and output shape, but never\n35|  inheritance;\n36|- the assay fork had repository tool access, so it could answer from disk while\n37|  the base was false;\n38|- the builder attestation accepted a correctly-shaped forged digest that the\n39|  caller minted itself;\n40|- clearance enforcement existed but no production path called it, and counting\n41|  tests around a fake proved nothing;\n42|- an unknown assay event preserved a false zero-tool observation;\n43|- a provider capability was declared absent to disable a flaky check, and the\n44|  claim did not reproduce (9/11 success).\n45|\n46|## Standard Negative Shapes\n47|\n48|Use these names in checklists, verdicts, and test names. They are the shapes a\n49|negative test must cover and the shapes a reviewer looks for first.\n50|\n51|| Shape | What it looks like when nobody tests for it | What the negative test must do |\n52|| --- | --- | --- |\n53|| Forged or self-minted evidence | The caller supplies the proof that the gate checks, and a correctly-shaped value passes. | Mint the evidence in the test the way a caller could, and require refusal. |\n54|| Absent evidence treated as satisfied | Missing input takes the permissive branch; the suite only ever supplies the input. | Remove the evidence entirely and require refusal, not a default-pass. |\n55|| Check present but uncalled from production | The guard is implemented and unit-tested by direct call; no production path invokes it. | Drive the real entry point — launch, materialize, resolve, publish — and name the production call site. |\n56|| Bypass path around the check | One entry point enforces; a second, older, or retry/renewal path does not. | Exercise every entry point that reaches the protected state, including retry, renewal, resume, and recovery, and every delivery surface that carries the rule — a contract clause reaching one context profile and not the other is this shape. |\n57|| Capability claim that does not reproduce | A capability is declared absent or present to make a flaky check go away. | Re-run the claim enough times to state a real rate, or report unknown. |\n58|\n59|## Derive Completeness From An Independent Source\n60|\n61|Completeness is derived from the pinned source or generated artifact, never\n62|enumerated by hand. When a registry, schema set, or declared scope defines the\n63|members, derive the expected set from that source and fail when any member lacks\n64|enforcement. This rule comes from five consecutive review rounds that each\n65|closed exactly the hand-picked members named by the previous reviewer; the next\n66|unlisted member defeated every list.\n67|\n68|A completeness test that reads the implementation's own table is circular and\n69|can never detect a missing entry: removing the entry also removes it from the\n70|test's expected set. Derive the expectation from the normative source of truth,\n71|not from the code under test. This distinction was what let the next Story's\n72|round-1 review demand a source-derived completeness test instead of accepting\n73|the producer's two selected cases.\n74|\n75|## Prove Exact Bounds At The Production Entry\n76|\n77|Prove every bound in both directions at the production entry: accept at the\n78|limit and refuse past the limit. Character bounds count characters rather than\n79|bytes. The motivating failure was a value containing 3,999 characters but\n80|5,999 bytes that production rejected with a byte comparison even though the\n81|normative `string[1..4096]` bound permitted it; helper-only or ASCII-only tests\n82|could not expose that narrowing.\n83|\n84|## Disable Every Refusal Clause\n85|\n86|Disable each refusal clause individually. If the suite stays green, that clause\n87|is a hole unless the test or evidence documents it as provably subsumed and\n88|names the check that subsumes it. This is measured rather than hypothetical: in\n89|one file, disabling 110 clause sites produced 45 surviving mutants, and 12 of\n90|those survivors were genuine widenings.\n91|\n92|Numeric-bound mutation and clause-disablement are different classes, and one\n93|harness rarely generates both. Numeric mutation finds off-by-one defects but\n94|cannot express disabling a tagged-union arm, cross-field equality, or grammar\n95|predicate; clause disablement finds those omissions but cannot move a numeric\n96|boundary. The 110-site clause run exposed widenings that the numeric harness\n97|could not generate, so run both classes.\n98|\n99|## Check Refusals Against The Normative Source\n100|\n101|A green test can defend a bug when it asserts a refusal that the normative\n102|source does not require. One observed test required production to reject values\n103|that the pinned specification permitted, so the suite protected the narrowing\n104|instead of detecting it. Whenever a test encodes a refusal, check that refusal\n105|against the pinned source rather than copying current behaviour into the\n106|assertion.\n107|\n108|## Eliminate Ambient Test Inputs\n109|\n110|No test may depend on ambient environment. Fixtures set explicit identity and\n111|all other values that could otherwise come from global configuration, the OS,\n112|or developer-machine state. A developer machine let Git derive an author name\n113|from the OS and passed the suite, while a CI runner with an empty GECOS field\n114|failed with `empty ident name`; only CI can catch this class, so the fixture\n115|must make its identity deterministic before CI exercises it.\n116|\n117|## Prove A Bound By Narrowing, Not By Deleting\n118|\n119|A test that removes a gate entirely proves only that the gate exists. It says\n120|nothing about whether the gate covers the right class. Restrict the gate to a\n121|narrower condition instead and require a named test to fail.\n122|\n123|Two repository incidents where a narrowed gate survived a green suite:\n124|\n125|- **BUG-260801-3kiloe F1** — the recovery successor cap was proven only by total\n126|  removal. Narrowing it to provider-limit signals left every other recoverable\n127|  failure unbounded, with the whole suite still green.\n128|- **TASK-260802-17wetr F16** — thirteen cycles later, the same shape: the\n129|  probe-lease cap survived deletion tests while the renewal path escaped it.\n130|- **TASK-260730-2c1e8l cycle 1** — this contract itself. The reviewer clauses\n131|  landed in the role body and the shipped test checked the role file and the\n132|  lite template separately, so both halves were green while the composed lite\n133|  prompt carried neither. Assert on the composed production artifact, not on the\n134|  pieces it is built from.\n135|- **TASK-260730-2c1e8l cycle 2** — the same contract, one level up, and the\n136|  clearest statement of the difference between the two shapes. The cycle-1 fix\n137|  did assert on the composed prompt, but it called the composition helper\n138|  directly and handed it the role, task-class filter, and profile itself.\n139|  Production builds those inputs inside the spawn entry point, so a mutant\n140|  narrowing only the real lite-reviewer routing just before composition left the\n141|  test green while an actual lite reviewer lost its gate-defeat licence. A test\n142|  that supplies the inputs is testing the helper, not the path. Obtain the\n143|  artifact the way the consumer does — here, read the prompt file recorded on\n144|  the run manifest after driving the entry point — so role resolution, the\n145|  task-class filter, and profile resolution are all under test rather than\n146|  assumed.\n147|\n148|Three traps when running the mutants themselves, all hit while proving this file:\n149|\n150|- **The mutant must be re-run with `-count=1`.** `go test` caches on package\n151|  sources; a test that reads `.roles/*.md` or any file outside its package at\n152|  runtime returns a stale cached PASS after that file is mutated. A cached green\n153|  is not a surviving mutant, it is an unexecuted test.\n154|- **A passing assertion may be satisfied by the wrong source.** Two mutants of\n155|  the producer DoD entries survived because the phrase asserted also appears,\n156|  differently worded, in the shared spawn template. Choose assertion wording\n157|  that only the intended source can supply, then narrow that source and require\n158|  the named test to fail.\n159|- **Restore the mutant from a copy, not from git.** `git checkout <file>`\n160|  restores from the index, which silently discards uncommitted work in that file\n161|  — during this task it reverted the whole cycle-2 change, not just the mutant.\n162|  Copy the file aside before mutating, restore from the copy, and verify the\n163|  restoration by diffing against it before rerunning the gates.\n164|\n165|## A Gate Publishes Its Coverage As A Ratio\n166|\n167|Prose about what a gate checks cannot distinguish 7 of 7 from 3 of 7. Every\n168|statement such a description makes is usually true — it is true of what the gate\n169|can see, and silent about what it cannot. The longer and more careful the\n170|description, the more thorough the gate looks.\n171|\n172|Report the fraction of intended targets the gate actually reaches, and assert\n173|that fraction so it reddens when a target drops out of reach. A target no mutant\n174|can redden is not covered, however elaborate the structure around it.\n175|\n176|Three defects of this exact shape, each found only once a ratio existed:\n177|\n178|- an AST call graph that recorded an edge only for a direct identifier call\n179|  covered 3 of 7 guarded functions while every pin passed; the package's real\n180|  dispatch was a function-value table, and the blind spot was invisible from\n181|  inside;\n182|- a classifier keyed on prose that a sibling gate was actively rewriting silently\n183|  dropped 8 rows, taking a suite from 107 executed subtests to 66, while its\n184|  completeness check `count == 0` reported nothing, because four is not zero;\n185|- an ownership gate that proved a symbol exists and a case is linked reported 48\n186|  sections as owned; measured against the specification, those bindings\n187|  discharged 2 of 394 normative clauses.\n188|\n189|A non-empty check on a derived set is the recurring form. `len(x) > 0` answers a\n190|different question from `len(x) == expected`, and only the second notices a\n191|narrowing.\n192|\n193|## A Blind Spot Is Not An Empty Set\n194|\n195|\"Nothing is there\" and \"nothing this checker can see\" are different facts, and\n196|only the second is a statement about the checker. Reporting the first when you\n197|mean the second converts a limitation into a clean bill of health, and the reader\n198|has no way to tell.\n199|\n200|An ownership gate scanned for uppercase RFC 2119 keywords. Sections stating their\n201|obligations in declarative present tense scored zero, were bucketed as carrying\n202|no obligations, and were admitted with no evidence required. Its documentation\n203|said \"there is no obligation to enumerate\". The true sentence was \"the section\n204|carries no keyword line, so the scanner cannot see its obligations\" — and 19 of\n205|151 headings were free-admission surface the moment they were bound, including a\n206|19-row exit-code registry and a closed manifest specification.\n207|\n208|Two rules follow:\n209|\n210|- State the bound of what the checker can see, next to what it reports. A\n211|  residual class that is named can be attacked later; one that is implied cannot.\n212|- Do not let the bucket for \"nothing to check\" also be the bucket that skips the\n213|  check. Where absence of measurable obligation is a legitimate state, require an\n214|  explicit reviewed justification for it, so the weakest entries are the ones\n215|  that must say the most rather than the least.\n216|\n217|## An Absence And A Failure To Read Are Different Facts\n218|\n219|Absence is a legitimate state with a defined fallback. A failed, partial, or\n220|malformed read is evidence of a problem. Treating the second as the first lets\n221|the fallback launder a fault into a normal-looking value, and a fallback defined\n222|for absence must never fire on a read failure.\n223|\n224|Each of these was a separate defect in this repository:\n225|\n226|- a non-empty value read as verified;\n227|- an unknown scanner version read as clean;\n228|- a partial provenance record read as absent;\n229|- a zero pid start time read as alive;\n230|- a malformed `api_error_status` read as missing;\n231|- an unparsed envelope read as no envelope — this one produced a false provider\n232|  suppression that would have hidden a healthy provider for hours.\n233|\n234|## Prove, Or Report Nothing\n235|\n236|Where a property cannot be established, report unparsed or unknown rather than\n237|inferring it from a proxy signal. A plausible guess is worse than an explicit\n238|unknown, because callers act on it.\n239|\n240|Incident: headless top-level inference in the Claude classifier was unsound in\n241|principle and produced six variants before it was deleted rather than\n242|strengthened.\n243|\n244|## Many Variants, One Unowned Decision\n245|\n246|A long run of same-shaped variants usually means a decision has more than one\n247|owner, not that there are many bugs. Eleven framing variants stopped reproducing\n248|only when structure got a single scanner and a single state type; every per-site\n249|patch before that produced the next variant. The operative wording is in\n250|`.roles/orchestrator/role.md`: unify the decision, do not patch each site.\n251|\n252|## Reviewer Licence\n253|\n254|Reviewers are explicitly licensed to attempt to defeat a gate and to reject a\n255|change whose only evidence is positive-path. Grep for callers before believing a\n256|guard is in force. The operative wording is in `.roles/reviewer/role.md`.","final_result":true}}}
