 with an empty GECOS field\n114|failed with `empty ident name`; only CI can catch this class, so the fixture\n115|must make its identity deterministic before CI exercises it.\n116|\n117|## Prove A Bound By Narrowing, Not By Deleting\n118|\n119|A test that removes a gate entirely proves only that the gate exists. It says\n120|nothing about whether the gate covers the right class. Restrict the gate to a\n121|narrower condition instead and require a named test to fail.\n122|\n123|Two repository incidents where a narrowed gate survived a green suite:\n124|\n125|- **BUG-260801-3kiloe F1** — the recovery successor cap was proven only by total\n126|  removal. Narrowing it to provider-limit signals left every other recoverable\n127|  failure unbounded, with the whole suite still green.\n128|- **TASK-260802-17wetr F16** — thirteen cycles later, the same shape: the\n129|  probe-lease cap survived deletion tests while the renewal path escaped it.\n130|- **TASK-260730-2c1e8l cycle 1** — this contract itself. The reviewer clauses\n131|  landed in the role body and the shipped test checked the role file and the\n132|  lite template separately, so both halves were green while the composed lite\n133|  prompt carried neither. Assert on the composed production artifact, not on the\n134|  pieces it is built from.\n135|- **TASK-260730-2c1e8l cycle 2** — the same contract, one level up, and the\n136|  clearest statement of the difference between the two shapes. The cycle-1 fix\n137|  did assert on the composed prompt, but it called the composition helper\n138|  directly and handed it the role, task-class filter, and profile itself.\n139|  Production builds those inputs inside the spawn entry point, so a mutant\n140|  narrowing only the real lite-reviewer routing just before composition left the\n141|  test green while an actual lite reviewer lost its gate-defeat licence. A test\n142|  that supplies the inputs is testing the helper, not the path. Obtain the\n143|  artifact the way the consumer does — here, read the prompt file recorded on\n144|  the run manifest after driving the entry point — so role resolution, the\n145|  task-class filter, and profile resolution are all under test rather than\n146|  assumed.\n147|\n148|Three traps when running the mutants themselves, all hit while proving this file:\n149|\n150|- **The mutant must be re-run with `-count=1`.** `go test` caches on package\n151|  sources; a test that reads `.roles/*.md` or any file outside its package at\n152|  runtime returns a stale cached PASS after that file is mutated. A cached green\n153|  is not a surviving mutant, it is an unexecuted test.\n154|- **A passing assertion may be satisfied by the wrong source.** Two mutants of\n155|  the producer DoD entries survived because the phrase asserted also appears,\n156|  differently worded, in the shared spawn template. Choose assertion wording\n157|  that only the intended source can supply, then narrow that source and require\n158|  the named test to fail.\n159|- **Restore the mutant from a copy, not from git.** `git checkout <file>`\n160|  restores from the index, which silently discards uncommitted work in that file\n161|  — during this task it reverted the whole cycle-2 change, not just the mutant.\n162|  Copy the file aside before mutating, restore from the copy, and verify the\n163|  restoration by diffing against it before rerunning the gates.\n164|\n165|## A Gate Publishes Its Coverage As A Ratio\n166|\n167|Prose about what a gate checks cannot distinguish 7 of 7 from 3 of 7. Every\n168|statement such a description makes is usually true — it is true of what the gate\n169|can see, and silent about what it cannot. The longer and more careful the\n170|description, the more thorough the gate looks.\n171|\n172|Report the fraction of intended targets the gate actually reaches, and assert\n173|that fraction so it reddens when a target drops out of reach. A target no mutant\n174|can redden is not covered, however elaborate the structure around it.\n175|\n176|Three defects of this exact shape, each found only once a ratio existed:\n177|\n178|- an AST call graph that recorded an edge only for a direct identifier call\n179|  covered 3 of 7 guarded functions while every pin passed; the package's real\n180|  dispatch was a function-value table, and the blind spot was invisible from\n181|  inside;\n182|- a classifier keyed on prose that a sibling gate was actively rewriting silently\n183|  dropped 8 rows, taking a suite from 107 executed subtests to 66, while its\n184|  completeness check `count == 0` reported nothing, because four is not zero;\n185|- an ownership gate that proved a symbol exists and a case is linked reported 48\n186|  sections as owned; measured against the specification, those bindings\n187|  discharged 2 of 394 normative clauses.\n188|\n189|A non-empty check on a derived set is the recurring form. `len(x) > 0` answers a\n190|different question from `len(x) == expected`, and only the second notices a\n191|narrowing.\n192|\n193|## A Blind Spot Is Not An Empty Set\n194|\n195|\"Nothing is there\" and \"nothing this checker can see\" are different facts, and\n196|only the second is a statement about the checker. Reporting the first when you\n197|mean the second converts a limitation into a clean bill of health, and the reader\n198|has no way to tell.\n199|\n200|An ownership gate scanned for uppercase RFC 2119 keywords. Sections stating their\n201|obligations in declarative present tense scored zero, were bucketed as carrying\n202|no obligations, and were admitted with no evidence required. Its documentation\n203|said \"there is no obligation to enumerate\". The true sentence was \"the section\n204|carries no keyword line, so the scanner cannot see its obligations\" — and 19 of\n205|151 headings were free-admission surface the moment they were bound, including a\n206|19-row exit-code registry and a closed manifest specification.\n207|\n208|Two rules follow:\n209|\n210|- State the bound of what the checker can see, next to what it reports. A\n211|  residual class that is named can be attacked later; one that is implied cannot.\n212|- Do not let the bucket for \"nothing to check\" also be the bucket that skips the\n213|  check. Where absence of measurable obligation is a legitimate state, require an\n214|  explicit reviewed justification for it, so the weakest entries are the ones\n215|  that must say the most rather than the least.\n216|\n217|## An Absence And A Failure To Read Are Different Facts\n218|\n219|Absence is a legitimate state with a defined fallback. A failed, partial, or\n220|malformed read is evidence of a problem. Treating the second as the first lets\n221|the fallback launder a fault into a normal-looking value, and a fallback defined\n222|for absence must never fire on a read failure.\n223|\n224|Each of these was a separate defect in this repository:\n225|\n226|- a non-empty value read as verified;\n227|- an unknown scanner version read as clean;\n228|- a partial provenance record read as absent;\n229|- a zero pid start time read as alive;\n230|- a malformed `api_error_status` read as missing;\n231|- an unparsed envelope read as no envelope — this one produced a false provider\n232|  suppression that would have hidden a healthy provider for hours.\n233|\n234|## Prove, Or Report Nothing\n235|\n236|Where a property cannot be established, report unparsed or unknown rather than\n237|inferring it from a proxy signal. A plausible guess is worse than an explicit\n238|unknown, because callers act on it.\n239|\n240|Incident: headless top-level inference in the Claude classifier was unsound in\n241|principle and produced six variants before it was deleted rather than\n242|strengthened.\n243|\n244|## Many Variants, One Unowned Decision\n245|\n246|A long run of same-shaped variants usually means a decision has more than one\n247|owner, not that there are many bugs. Eleven framing variants stopped reproducing\n248|only when structure got a single scanner and a single state type; every per-site\n249|patch before that produced the next variant. The operative wording is in\n250|`.roles/orchestrator/role.md`: unify the decision, do not patch each site.\n251|\n252|## Reviewer Licence\n253|\n254|Reviewers are explicitly licensed to attempt to defeat a gate and to reject a\n255|change whose only evidence is positive-path. Grep for callers before believing a\n256|guard is in force. The operative wording is in `.roles/reviewer/role.md`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
