{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d4f5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adca-fe2f-74a0-ad0c-d5a68eb484bd"},"sequence":2261,"recorded_at":1780531400004517,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05bf7ae6-0f62-48b6-bcc1-cef4e9824e8d"},"call_id":"call_01a0add9a8e67258a09d74dec92b652d","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-51-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n 19,120p internal/axerror/details.go; echo ===; grep -n 'func ExitCodeFor' -A 20 internal/axerror/registry.go | head -30\",\n  \"description\": \"Read detail validation and exit resolution\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"type Details map[string]any\\n\\nvar (\\n\\t// ErrInvalidDetails reports a diagnostic map outside the Section 15.1\\n\\t// shape, bounds, or redaction rules.\\n\\tErrInvalidDetails = errors.New(\\\"invalid structured error details\\\")\\n\\n\\t// ErrCausalLeak reports human text or a diagnostic value that reproduces\\n\\t// the rendered text of the Go cause the failure was built from. The cause\\n\\t// chain stays local; it is never copied onto the wire.\\n\\tErrCausalLeak = errors.New(\\\"structured error would carry its cause onto the wire\\\")\\n)\\n\\n// detailKeyPattern is the Section 15.1 constraint on detail keys, verbatim:\\n// \\\"0-64 keys matching [a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}\\\".\\nvar detailKeyPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}$`)\\n\\nconst (\\n\\tmaxDetailKeys      = 64\\n\\tmaxDetailDepth     = 4\\n\\tmaxDetailCanonical = 16 * 1024\\n\\tminRedactableCause = 8\\n\\tmaxMessageRunes    = 4096\\n\\tminMessageRunes    = 1\\n)\\n\\n// excludedDetailKeys is the best-effort scanner Section 16.2 says an\\n// implementation SHOULD offer. It refuses a detail key that names one of the\\n// four classes Section 15.1 forbids outright — \\\"No detail may contain a\\n// credential, raw transcript, environment secret, or opaque bundle content\\\" —\\n// and nothing else.\\n//\\n// Matching is exact, never by substring, and that is deliberate. A substring\\n// rule refusing every key containing \\\"token\\\", \\\"socket\\\" or \\\"credential\\\" would\\n// refuse \\\"token_count\\\", \\\"socket_timeout_ms\\\" and \\\"credential_profile\\\" — ordinary\\n// diagnostics the specification admits — while still passing a secret written\\n// under an innocuous name. That is pure false-positive surface with no\\n// true-positive capability, and it is the exact defect removed from the\\n// Configuration extension-key validator: where the pinned document is silent\\n// about a name, be permissive.\\n//\\n// The list is also scoped to Section 15.1's four classes rather than to the\\n// whole Section 16.2 exclusion table. Section 16.2 governs manifests and\\n// bundles generated by ax; a diagnostic key naming a PID, a tmux socket or a\\n// Terminal Instance Binding is not a credential, a transcript, an environment\\n// secret, or bundle content, and refusing it here would invent a constraint the\\n// error contract does not state.\\nvar excludedDetailKeys = map[string]string{\\n\\t// Credential.\\n\\t\\\"access_token\\\":       \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"api_key\\\":            \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"auth_json\\\":          \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"cookie\\\":             \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"cookies\\\":            \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"credential\\\":         \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"credentials\\\":        \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"oauth_token\\\":        \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"passphrase\\\":         \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"password\\\":           \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"private_key\\\":        \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"refresh_token\\\":      \\\"credential\\\",\\n\\t\\\"session_token\\\":      \\\"credential\\\"