ive path; two new vocabulary\\n  derivations (`resumeProviders` from the Section 8.2 table,\\n  `discoveryMembers` from the Section 7.5 type row).\\n- MUTANTS: shipped `internal/provhost/testdata/mutate_identity.py`\\n  reports 24/24 applied N plants killed on the exact final source\\n  (two token-preserving: opaque `/` suffix-swap, muse `0.1.0`\\n  admission), harmless control `SURVIVED`, `NOT_APPLIED` and\\n  `COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE` outside the numerator. The first\\n  battery run caught two inverted mutant conditions before they\\n  shipped.\\n- IDEMPOTENCY: `TestCreateIdentityIsByteIdentical` proves 25\\n  identical emissions; creation is pure with no durable writes, so\\n  crash/restart evidence is a stated bound, not a gap.\\n- BOUNDS: Section 2.4 profile authority stays sibling-owned\\n  (TASK-260830-3uzfyn); version ranges stay opaque; only Muse\\n  carries a cell-level version pin; no CLI or capability\\n  advertisement added. Coverage 9 of 10 AC rows driven plus the\\n  crash bound; see `internal/provhost/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- HANDOFF: results, conformance matrix, and producer evidence\\n  tarball attached to the task; candidate left uncommitted.\\n...\\n1:# Flight Logbook\\n6:## 2026-09-17\\n8:### TASK-260830-kp4zpu — provider identity creation and binding\\n42:### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\\n77:### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev15 rework: close seal/token path and callback provenance census gaps\\n102:## 2026-09-16\\n104:### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev11 rework: referenced checkpoint admitted through the shared semantic owner\\n134:### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev10 rework: fork/resume profile authority closed by relation census\\n186:## 2026-09-10\\n188:### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev8 rework: checkpoint profile authority admitted over the event-head closure\\n241:### TASK-260830-21gygk rev4 rework: winning-lease succession, parked fail-closed, closed capability vocabulary\\n277:## 2026-09-09\\n279:### TASK-260830-21gygk rework: all four rev2 review findings implemented in the shared selector layer\\n330:### TASK-260830-21gygk resume: re-validated v0.6.0 selector candidate, one doc-accuracy fix\\n350:### TASK-260908-2tkufa: recovered v0.6.0 consumer adoption and bound pending runtime owners\\n359:### TASK-260908-3kvnm2: adopted signed v0.6.0 normative source alongside v0.5.0, no consumer re-pointed\\n367:## 2026-09-08\\n369:### TASK-260830-1r9wrr: missing Type-ownership gate before R2-F2 rework\\n377:## 2026-09-07\\n379:### TASK-260830-1r9wrr rev2: F1/F2/F4/F5/F6 repaired; F3 and F7 Local remained open\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3542,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 886,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
